, selling stationery, and turning private grievances into carefully chosen public words. Show ink-black fingertips, lead type cases, drying sheets, patched press belt. A customer counter separates the shopfront from type cases, a hand-fed press, and a drying room. A rear desk holds drafts and correspondence; proofs may be pinned publicly only when marked for release. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo. Compose around this location’s own architecture, furnishings and landscape. Keep the railway bridge outside the frame; windows show nearby buildings, vegetation or sky.","visualAnchors":["ink-black fingertips","lead type cases","drying sheets","patched press belt"],"avoid":["modern objects","readable private papers","railway bridge in background","repeated town panorama"],"railwayBridgeVisible":false},"canonical_lore":{"version":2,"authored":true,"summary":"A working print shop publishing The Run Ledger, selling stationery, and turning private grievances into carefully chosen public words.","publicHistory":["Iris purchased a damaged press with savings and an equipment loan. The shop’s older job-printing business pays for a newspaper whose independence is admired more often than it is financially supported."],"sensoryDetails":["ink-black fingertips","lead type cases","drying sheets","patched press belt"],"layout":["A customer counter separates the shopfront from type cases, a hand-fed press, and a drying room. A rear desk holds drafts and correspondence; proofs may be pinned publicly only when marked for release."],"localEtiquette":["Do not touch type or lift private proofs. Published assertions can be questioned; unpublished material requires Iris’s permission."],"stableFacts":["A working print shop publishing The Run Ledger, selling stationery, and turning private grievances into carefully chosen public words."],"conversationHooks":["printing","news discussion","notice submission","proofreading by invita