d cargo bays","water barrel","faded route board"],"avoid":["modern objects","readable private papers","railway bridge in background","repeated town panorama"],"railwayBridgeVisible":false},"canonical_lore":{"version":2,"authored":true,"summary":"An old relay station that gives independent carriers a place to change animals, leave agreed consignments, and weigh how much they need to know.","publicHistory":["The route once served Calder’s original circuit. Railway speculation revived it for deliveries that benefit from flexibility, lower fees, or less attention."],"sensoryDetails":["old freight timbers","numbered cargo bays","water barrel","faded route board"],"layout":["A public receiving bench faces the yard. Assigned cargo bays, animal areas, route records, and Eve’s living room are separately controlled. A private cache is never automatically visible."],"localEtiquette":["A delivery agreement specifies what is carried and who may collect it. Private cargo and a rider’s personal history are not public property."],"stableFacts":["An old relay station that gives independent carriers a place to change animals, leave agreed consignments, and weigh how much they need to know."],"conversationHooks":["courier arrangements","animal changes","route discussion","shelter by agreement"],"storySeeds":[]}},{"id":"38b0efd4-b1d9-5b32-bc1f-b0b711da47ca","world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","parent_location_id":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","name":"The Red Sash","slug":"red-sash-brothel","description":"The Red Sash is a working brothel with a lively downstairs parlor, adult resident workers, and a practical struggle over how its profits and rules should be shared.","category":"brothel","location_type":"venue","sort_order":510,"depth":1,"visual_asset_key":"calders-run-red-sash-brothel","hours":{"open":"16:00","close":"02:00"},"possible_activities":["adult social company","music","agreed private appointments","resident business meetings"],"access_metadata":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true,"publicMapVisible":true},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","district":"lantern-row","assetStatus":"pending","photoStatus":"pending","userLocalClock":true,"publicMapVisible":true},"canonical_visual_context":{"canonicalPrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. The Red Sash: The Red Sash is a working brothel with a lively downstairs parlor, adult resident workers, and a practical struggle over how its profits and rules should be shared. Show red sash above the entry, warm plaster parlor, upright music stand, separate residential stair. A public adult parlor and small music area lead to a staffed reception point. Private service rooms require a particular worker’s agreement. Resident bedrooms, the accounts desk, and the back kitchen are not public extensions of the parlor. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo. Compose around this location’s own architecture, furnishings and landscape. Keep the railway bridge outside the frame; windows show nearby buildings, vegetation or sky.","visualAnchors":["red sash above the entry","warm plaster parlor","upright music stand","separate residential stair"],"avoid":["modern objects","readable private papers","railway bridge in background","repeated town panorama"],"railwayBridgeVisible":false},"canonical_lore":{"version":2,"authored":true,"summary":"The Red Sash is a working brothel with a lively downstairs parlor, adult resident workers, and a practical struggle over how its profits and rules should be shared.","publicHistory":["The building began as a merchant’s lodging house and changed use as Lantern Row expanded. A nonresident owner collects rent and fees through a management agreement; Sabine and Bess want the resident workers to gain a meaningful say in that agreement."],"sensoryDetails":["red sash above the entry","warm plaster parlor","upright music stand","separate residential stair"],"layout":["A public adult parlor and small music area lead to a staffed reception point. Private service rooms require a particular worker’s agreement. Resident bedrooms, the accounts desk, and the back kitchen are not public extensions of the parlor."],"localEtiquette":["Every worker is an adult with independent choice over clients and services. Paid work does not create personal romantic availability. Bess and Sabine are unrelated coworkers, not siblings."],"stableFacts":["The Red Sash is a working brothel with a lively downstairs parlor, adult resident workers, and a practical struggle over how its profits and rules should be shared."],"conversationHooks":["adult social company","music","agreed private appointments","resident business meetings"],"storySeeds":[]}},{"id":"cd490e32-1392-5575-91ea-f8d60722de15","world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","parent_location_id":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","name":"Crowcut Hollow","slug":"crowcut-hollow","description":"Crowcut Hollow is a remote bandit hideout in a side canyon, built around an abandoned freight shelter and the uneasy domestic life of people living beyond ordinary protection.","category":"bandit hideout","location_type":"venue","sort_order":520,"depth":1,"visual_asset_key":"calders-run-crowcut-hollow","hours":{"open":"00:00","close":"24:00"},"possible_activities":["story-gated meetings","camp conversation","accountability negotiations","ordinary camp work"],"access_metadata":{"mode":"story_gated","initiallyDiscoverable":false,"requiredState":"crowcut.access_granted","privateAreasRequireInvitation":true,"publicMapVisible":false},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","district":"cinder-bluffs","assetStatus":"pending","photoStatus":"pending","userLocalClock":true,"publicMapVisible":false},"canonical_visual_context":{"canonicalPrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Crowcut Hollow: Crowcut Hollow is a remote bandit hideout in a side canyon, built around an abandoned freight shelter and the uneasy domestic life of people living beyond ordinary protection. Show weathered freight shelter, red canyon walls, patched blankets, small stable enclosure. The authored location contains a rough communal shelter, a stable enclosure, separate sleeping spaces, and a meeting area. Its precise discovery route is story-gated. No public map reveals entry merely because the player has heard the name. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo. Compose around this location’s own architecture, furnishings and landscape. Keep the railway bridge outside the frame; windows show nearby buildings, vegetation or sky.","visualAnchors":["weathered freight shelter","red canyon walls","patched blankets","small stable enclosure"],"avoid":["modern objects","readable private papers","railway bridge in background","repeated town panorama"],"railwayBridgeVisible":false},"canonical_lore":{"version":2,"authored":true,"summary":"Crowcut Hollow is a remote bandit hideout in a side canyon, built around an abandoned freight shelter and the uneasy domestic life of people living beyond ordinary protection.","publicHistory":[],"sensoryDetails":["weathered freight shelter","red canyon walls","patched blankets","small stable enclosure"],"layout":["The authored location contains a rough communal shelter, a stable enclosure, separate sleeping spaces, and a meeting area. Its precise discovery route is story-gated. No public map reveals entry merely because the player has heard the name."],"localEtiquette":["Entry requires discovery and an authored access state. An invitation to the communal shelter does not open private sleeping spaces or personal papers. Visitors can decline a meeting or leave; romance does not oblige anyone to join the crew."],"stableFacts":["Crowcut Hollow is a remote bandit hideout in a side canyon, built around an abandoned freight shelter and the uneasy domestic life of people living beyond ordinary protection."],"conversationHooks":["story-gated meetings","camp conversation","accountability negotiations","ordinary camp work"],"storySeeds":[]}}]'::jsonb) as r(id uuid,world_id uuid,parent_location_id uuid,name text,slug text,description text,category text,location_type text,sort_order integer,depth smallint,visual_asset_key text,hours jsonb,possible_activities text[],access_metadata jsonb,metadata jsonb,canonical_visual_context jsonb,canonical_lore jsonb) on conflict(id) do update set world_id=excluded.world_id,parent_location_id=excluded.parent_location_id,name=excluded.name,slug=excluded.slug,description=excluded.description,category=excluded.category,location_type=excluded.location_type,sort_order=excluded.sort_order,depth=excluded.depth,visual_asset_key=excluded.visual_asset_key,hours=excluded.hours,possible_activities=excluded.possible_activities,access_metadata=excluded.access_metadata,metadata=excluded.metadata || coalesce((select jsonb_object_agg(key,value) from jsonb_each(together_locations.metadata) where key=any(array['assetStatus','photoStatus'])),'{}'::jsonb),canonical_visual_context=excluded.canonical_visual_context,canonical_lore=excluded.canonical_lore;

