se,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Keene’s Print Shop: A working print shop publishing The Run Ledger, selling stationery, and turning private grievances into carefully chosen public words. Show ink-black fingertips, lead type cases, drying sheets, patched press belt. A customer counter separates the shopfront from type cases, a hand-fed press, and a drying room. A rear desk holds drafts and correspondence; proofs may be pinned publicly only when marked for release. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-keenes-print-shop","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:12a6914f-0fe4-544d-bfe9-b36c97ea81e8","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"12a6914f-0fe4-544d-bfe9-b36c97ea81e8","authoringNumber":3,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"county-courthouse","name":"County Courthouse","nodeType":"place","parentLocationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","category":"courthouse","publicSummary":"The county’s modest record office and hearing rooms, where property, inheritance, and public promises acquire forms that outlast the people arguing over them.","history":"A reading room became a courthouse as the town grew. Reconstruction after the flood left an uneven archive: some volumes survived, some were copied, and some entries remain disputed.","layout":"A public counter and notice board lead to a hearing room. Copy desks occupy a bright side room. The archive cage, evidence cupboard, and officials’ offices require specific access.","socialTexture":"Mornings are procedural and crowded; afternoons slow into document work. Adult evening petition clinics happen only on authored dates, with Esther or a supervising official present.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"A copied water-register page combines measurements from different years. Its existence is genuine; whether its use was fraudulent requires comparison with other evidence.","storySeeds":["A claimant needs an accurate copy before a hearing.","A missing page is less revealing than the filing date of the page replacing it."],"activities":["record requests","public hearings","petition assistance","archive research"],"visualAnchors":["sunlit copy desk","uneven brick addition","locked iron cage","crowded notice board"],"etiquette":"Public records and sealed records have different access. Clerks can explain process but cannot promise a ruling or create legal authority.","primaryCharacterIds":["17799880-e679-5080-b921-b9f4afa3b6fb"],"regularCharacterIds":["17799880-e679-5080-b921-b9f4afa3b6fb","dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a","8d8a8b9e-aac5-5c86-883c-e55d5c1245ba"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. County Courthouse: The county’s modest record office and hearing rooms, where property, inheritance, and public promises acquire forms that outlast the people arguing over them. Show sunlit copy desk, uneven brick addition, locked iron cage, crowded notice board. A public counter and notice board lead to a hearing room. Copy desks occupy a bright side room. The archive cage, evidence cupboard, and officials’ offices require specific access. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-county-courthouse","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:602be10b-b09b-58df-965e-033a1ea401d8","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"602be10b-b09b-58df-965e-033a1ea401d8","authoringNumber":4,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"dempsey-livery","name":"Dempsey Livery","nodeType":"place","parentLocationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","category":"livery stable","publicSummary":"A busy livery and training yard where the town hires transport, boards animals, swaps practical news, and learns whether a newcomer can be trusted with a horse.","history":"June’s family built the yard around coach traffic. Growing debt and the railway’s arrival have made its future uncertain, but its repair contacts and sound animals remain indispensable.","layout":"The hire counter faces a covered yard. Training pens, tack room, feed loft, and staff cottage sit beyond. Visitors wait at the rail until invited into an animal’s space.","socialTexture":"Dawn departures and evening returns are crowded. Midday offers training, grooming, and quieter conversation. A delayed return can disturb several people’s plans.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"A recently accepted boarding animal matches a disputed bill of sale. June knows the paperwork is weak but has not established who is telling the truth.","storySeeds":["A borrowed horse is recognized by someone who claims it was stolen.","A novice rider needs help before an important visit."],"activities":["horse hire","riding lessons","grooming","travel planning"],"visualAnchors":["dusty training rail","labeled tack hooks","hay loft","water trough"],"etiquette":"Animal welfare governs access and timing. Borrowing requires a specific agreement; being friendly with June does not make every horse available.","primaryCharacterIds":["db699624-91b3-5c34-93ec-53c7974498fb"],"regularCharacterIds":["db699624-91b3-5