ounter. A scale and invoice desk mark the boundary of the stockroom. The upstairs rooms are private storage and household space.","socialTexture":"Working customers arrive early; browsing and household shopping fill the afternoon. Near closing, Lottie rearranges displays and weighs what people asked for against what the owner will buy.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Lottie has designed a buying list for a small independent shop. She is using public catalog prices, not stealing the store’s accounts.","storySeeds":["A scarce delivery is promised to two customers.","A bold display succeeds, and someone else takes the credit."],"activities":["shopping","fabric selection","ordering supplies","parcel collection"],"visualAnchors":["fabric bolts","brass scale","hanging lanterns","scuffed freight counter"],"etiquette":"A store tab is a financial arrangement, not social ownership. Ask before opening stock drawers or reading an invoice.","primaryCharacterIds":["38c61131-14a4-5a14-9165-d307095419ba"],"regularCharacterIds":["38c61131-14a4-5a14-9165-d307095419ba","dbc7cf13-72ae-587a-b3d1-468ca2f132b1","2aedb376-b459-54f7-ae2e-4a2251f295c7"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"07:00","closes":"20:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Crown & Cotton Mercantile: The mercantile supplies everything from nails and lamp wicks to fabric, with a stockroom whose contents reveal the town’s changing ambitions. Show fabric bolts, brass scale, hanging lanterns, scuffed freight counter. Public aisles lead past hardware and dry goods to a fabric counter. A scale and invoice desk mark the boundary of the stockroom. The upstairs rooms are private storage and household space. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-crown-and-cotton","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:9fcae9c7-e773-534c-9ac7-7df82b66ae17","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"9fcae9c7-e773-534c-9ac7-7df82b66ae17","authoringNumber":6,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"hearthstone-bakery","name":"Hearthstone Bakery","nodeType":"place","parentLocationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","category":"bakery","publicSummary":"A warm bakery serving ordinary bread, occasional elaborate pastries, and a few tables whose regulars know the rhythms of the oven.","history":"The business survived the dry summer by shortening its menu and sharing deliveries. Beatrice learned the practical cost of wasting a batch and now balances affordable staples with higher-margin commissions.","layout":"A front counter and two small tables overlook the boardwalk. The oven room, mixing bench, and ingredient store sit behind a half door. Work space is tight and hot.","socialTexture":"The first hours are brisk with workers collecting breakfast. Afternoons grow companionable as the last loaves cool. A large special order can change the whole day.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Beatrice keeps a small, openly documented reduced-price shelf after the main rush. She is ashamed that she sometimes resents customers who assume the reduction is endless.","storySeeds":["A celebration order conflicts with supplying the boardinghouse.","Someone anonymously pays for another household’s weekly bread."],"activities":["breakfast","bread buying","pastry orders","kitchen conversation by invitation"],"visualAnchors":["flour-dusted counter","brick oven","window cooling rack","blue enamel pitcher"],"etiquette":"The kitchen requires permission. Help is useful when offered concretely, and a gift should not expose a recipient’s hardship.","prim