sk and benches occupy the front. A record cupboard, small interview room, and separate holding area are restricted. The back yard is used for maintenance and authorized transfers.","socialTexture":"Morning reports give way to patrols and appointments. Another officer may staff the desk when Elias is away, but background staff do not acquire a new named companion identity.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Elias has tolerated limited fee-evasion deliveries when household necessity was involved. His notes distinguish those cases, but the arrangement was never formally approved.","storySeeds":["An accusation relies on a witness who saw only part of an event.","A formerly harmless exception is invoked to excuse a serious theft."],"activities":["reporting a problem","public notices","lawful appointments","found-property claims"],"visualAnchors":["scarred desk","repair tools by a window","holding-room door","pinned notices"],"etiquette":"A notice is not proof of guilt. Restricted records and holding areas require actual authority; a personal relationship does not provide it.","primaryCharacterIds":["dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a"],"regularCharacterIds":["dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a","17799880-e679-5080-b921-b9f4afa3b6fb","dd646eaf-8983-567b-b3c5-00d4f5175b2c"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"00:00","closes":"24:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Marshal’s Office: The marshal’s small office combines public service, uncomfortable waiting, local records, and the persistent problem of deciding which trouble cannot wait. Show scarred desk, repair tools by a window, holding-room door, pinned notices. A desk and benches occupy the front. A record cupboard, small interview room, and separate holding area are restricted. The back yard is used for maintenance and authorized transfers. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-marshals-office","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:5bd7111c-2e34-5c40-9779-b4dd2aec21c3","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"5bd7111c-2e34-5c40-9779-b4dd2aec21c3","authoringNumber":8,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"soto-forge","name":"Soto Forge","nodeType":"place","parentLocationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","category":"forge and repair yard","publicSummary":"A forge and wagon yard where hot metal, measured workmanship, and friendly argument keep the town’s animals and vehicles moving.","history":"Gabriel acquired tools gradually and rents the yard. He has more demand than space, yet a move would mean leaving customers who can walk to the present shop and pay in small installments.","layout":"The public yard contains a waiting rail and repair wagons. A forge bay, tool wall, and small office sit under a broad roof. Hot work zones are kept clear.","socialTexture":"Morning jobs are organized around animals and departures. Afternoon repairs allow longer talk between noisy stretches. Friends gather after the fires are banked.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Gabriel has priced a new workshop near the railhead but has not told June because she would read the move as a judgment on the livery’s future.","storySeeds":["A repair mark can identify a wagon seen on an old road.","An attractive workshop offer would leave longstanding customers without affordable help."],"activities":["wagon repair","farrier work","tool discussion","after-work meals"],"visualAnchors":["forge glow","hanging horseshoes","half-repaired wagon","shared outdoor table"],"etiquette":"Wait for Gabriel to make work safe before 