e location partly because her work made it desirable.","layout":"The main bar opens to tables and a small music platform. A courtyard catches evening air. The back meeting room and upstairs lodgings require invitation; the office contains private business records.","socialTexture":"Afternoon trade is relaxed and conversational. Evenings draw mixed company. Closing is work: counting, cleaning, escorting staff, and settling disagreements without turning them into a spectacle.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Gin can purchase the building only with outside money. Halden’s associate wants approval over private bookings in return for favorable financing.","storySeeds":["A meeting booking forces Gin to choose between money and the room’s reputation.","A musician’s departure threatens a valued nightly routine."],"activities":["supper","music","conversation","private meetings by arrangement"],"visualAnchors":["copper horse above the bar","worn piano","courtyard lanterns","polished but repaired tables"],"etiquette":"Staff can refuse service. A drink buys a drink. Joining a table or entering the back room requires an invitation.","primaryCharacterIds":["9ed7daa2-a0a3-52cf-b7f4-ad8d220750ab"],"regularCharacterIds":["9ed7daa2-a0a3-52cf-b7f4-ad8d220750ab","ab4cfd68-d04d-5ebb-b874-e33648cca0c3","dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"12:00","closes":"02:00","overnight":true,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Copper Mare Saloon: The Copper Mare is a generous, noisy saloon with good music, ordinary food, and a back room where people who dislike one another sometimes manage to talk. Show copper horse above the bar, worn piano, courtyard lanterns, polished but repaired tables. The main bar opens to tables and a small music platform. A courtyard catches evening air. The back meeting room and upstairs l