f work can be busy after ordinary work hours. Quiet periods permit conversation if Jonah is present.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"A major donor wants private influence over the relief list. Jonah has postponed answering while depending on the money for winter supplies.","storySeeds":["A donation carries a condition that would exclude a neighbor.","Music brings together people who avoid one another elsewhere."],"activities":["worship","relief work","music","community suppers"],"visualAnchors":["plain wooden benches","small harmonium","relief kitchen","river-facing windows"],"etiquette":"Relief creates no obligation to worship or disclose private beliefs. Confidences and donation records require permission to share.","primaryCharacterIds":["be0f7849-8182-5ee7-bb81-03aa9c1ec5e9"],"regularCharacterIds":["be0f7849-8182-5ee7-bb81-03aa9c1ec5e9","2005abeb-d903-5a5a-a1cb-296fdd68b02a","de185ba5-cd6b-5022-80cd-8669cc8cfaf2"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"07:00","closes":"21:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Riverside Chapel: A small riverside chapel and relief hall where worship, music, practical aid, and disagreements about deservingness share the same benches. Show plain wooden benches, small harmonium, relief kitchen, river-facing windows. The nave opens to a multipurpose hall and shaded yard. Jonah’s office, donation records, and stored relief goods are restricted. The building is modest rather than monumental. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-riverside-chapel","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:61a778ab-001e-55f5-829c-2213f115f9a3","