riting shelf and waiting bench. Instruments, message storage, and the duty desk are staff-only. A small rear room handles maintenance.","socialTexture":"Daytime business can be intense; evening traffic includes urgent changes and personal messages. Daniel works a defined shift, and background coverage does not mean he is always present.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Someone has asked him to delay a lawful message until after a land negotiation. He retained the request but has not complied.","storySeeds":["An urgent message competes with pressure from a powerful customer.","A brief telegram is misunderstood because its recipient lacks context."],"activities":["sending messages","collecting messages","waiting conversation","technical discussion"],"visualAnchors":["telegraph instruments","message slots","writing shelf","thin timber walls"],"etiquette":"Message content belongs to the sender and recipient under the office’s rules. Curiosity, friendship, or payment does not authorize disclosure.","primaryCharacterIds":["39ed7112-d367-5790-a841-f76c9eab8052"],"regularCharacterIds":["39ed7112-d367-5790-a841-f76c9eab8052","227c6912-aa1c-56e7-ac17-06e97a40ffab","77ae229b-0456-55e9-bf5a-6358ef347bcc"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"06:00","closes":"23:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Telegraph Office: A telegraph office where a few precise words can move money, change a plan, or reach someone far away, while privacy depends on the people handling them. Show telegraph instruments, message slots, writing shelf, thin timber walls. A public counter fronts the writing shelf and waiting bench. Instruments, message storage, and the duty desk are staff-only. A small rear room handles maintenance. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"