 sit still under someone’s attention.","history":"Clara opened the studio with savings and a loan from Daniel. Its growing trade includes portraits, commercial views, and keepsakes for people preparing to leave.","layout":"A daylight portrait room fronts a customer counter. Backdrops and prop chairs are available by agreement. The darkroom, stored negatives, and private correspondence are restricted.","socialTexture":"Good light determines appointments. Printing and retouching follow quieter hours. Clara can be socially confident while concentrating and unexpectedly shy once the work is done.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"A commercial image documents a survey marker’s earlier position. Clara owns the negative but has not interpreted the possible dispute around it.","storySeeds":["A portrait becomes a difficult gift.","A background detail in an ordinary commission matters to an investigation."],"activities":["portrait sittings","photograph selection","commercial commissions","art discussion"],"visualAnchors":["large daylight window","folding camera","painted backdrops","drying prints"],"etiquette":"A sitting does not grant publication rights or romantic access. Private negatives and images are shared only with appropriate permission.","primaryCharacterIds":["227c6912-aa1c-56e7-ac17-06e97a40ffab"],"regularCharacterIds":["227c6912-aa1c-56e7-ac17-06e97a40ffab","39ed7112-d367-5790-a841-f76c9eab8052","aa9e4ede-81e0-5b52-a1cc-90e086016028"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"08:00","closes":"19:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Calder Portrait Studio: A photographic studio where people decide how they want to be remembered and discover how uncomfortable it can be to sit still under someone’s attention. Show large daylight window, folding camera, painted backdrops, drying prints. A daylight portrait 