mfortable house and productive land make independence look effortless to people who do not see its accounts.","history":"The Whitcomb holding grew through work, marriage, purchases, and advantageous water arrangements. Adelaide inherited a business with obligations as well as privilege and expanded it through demanding management.","layout":"A visitor gate leads to the office, work yard, and an agreed meeting porch. Grazing land, irrigation equipment, staff housing, and the family house have distinct access.","socialTexture":"Livestock and field work begin early. Business fills afternoon; invited suppers reveal a more relaxed household. Adelaide is not necessarily at the house when the ranch is operating.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"A smaller neighbor’s access relies on an informal promise Adelaide has treated as revocable. Her public defense of local rights makes the discrepancy politically sensitive.","storySeeds":["A daughter’s independence tests a parent’s generosity.","A neighbor asks that a remembered promise become a written guarantee."],"activities":["ranch business","invited riding","work-yard visits","household supper by invitation"],"visualAnchors":["broad shaded porch","irrigated pasture","working corrals","well-used ranch office"],"etiquette":"The ranch is a workplace and home. Business access never grants family-room or bedroom access; employees have obligations and limits of their own.","primaryCharacterIds":["8d8a8b9e-aac5-5c86-883c-e55d5c1245ba"],"regularCharacterIds":["8d8a8b9e-aac5-5c86-883c-e55d5c1245ba","dbc7cf13-72ae-587a-b3d1-468ca2f132b1","cffa45a6-3817-5f0d-9fde-3ec4ca76696a"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"06:00","closes":"20:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Whitcomb Ranch: A substantial working ranch whose comfortable house and productive land make independence look effortless to people who do not see its accounts. Show broad shaded porch, irrigated pasture, working corrals, well-used ranch office. A visitor gate leads to the office, work yard, and an agreed meeting porch. Grazing land, irrigation equipment, staff housing, and the family house have distinct access. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-whitcomb-ranch","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:65aa25c9-b4db-5710-8594-91642bddc294","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"65aa25c9-b4db-5710-8594-91642bddc294","authoringNumber":33,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"orchard-schoolhouse","name":"Orchard Schoolhouse","nodeType":"place","parentLocationId":"cff3d4a7-0a30-57e0-ba3f-d74db9b72810","category":"school and adult classroom","publicSummary":"A small schoolhouse whose adult evening classes and community meetings provide a place to ask a question without performing confidence.","history":"Local households built the first classroom together. Eliza now teaches daytime pupils offstage and organizes adult literacy sessions for workers whose schooling was interrupted.","layout":"The classroom opens to a shaded yard and a small staff room. Adult companion encounters occur in staff areas or scheduled adult sessions; children’s teaching is background world activity.","socialTexture":"Daytime school hours restrict casual visits. Adult classes and community use happen in explicit evening windows. Quiet preparation offers Eliza time she often forgets to protect.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Eliza has applied for funding to continue her own education. She fears residents will treat ambition as evidence that her care for the town was temporary.","storySeeds":["An adult learner wants help without becoming a public example.","A teacher’s opportunity to leave complicates a friendship or romance."],"activities":["adult literacy classes","community meetings","staff appointments","reading"],"visualAnchors":["plain desks","slate board","shaded schoolyard","crowded book cupboard"],"etiquette":"Adult scenes use adult-only sessions or staff areas. Student privacy is protected, and romantic scenes never include minors or their activities.","primaryCharacterIds":["fa092c09-c4c0-5ca4-8482-1c00cc7e5897"],"regularCharacterIds":["fa092c09-c4c0-5ca4-8482-1c00cc7e5897","0545674e-2ac8-540c-a0b2-ac6882fc4641","fe0749b0-c5c5-5fb0-825c-5faae2bb1360"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"08:00","closes":"20:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Orchard Schoolhouse: A small schoolhouse whose adult evening classes and community meetings provide a place to ask a question without performing confidence. Show plain desks, slate board, shaded schoolyard, crowded book cupboard. The classroom opens to a shaded yard and a small staff room. Adult companion encounters occur in staff areas or scheduled adult sessions; children’s teaching is background world activity. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-orchard-schoolhouse","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:d62ba68c-1c91-56e2-8cdd-de1b2507f0cb","content_type":"location_canon","knowledge_scope":"story","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"d62ba68c-1c91-56e2-8cdd-de1b2507f0cb","authoringNumber":34,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"cot