ence.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Several inherited priority entries are accurate copies of the compact yet produce unequal modern results. Other disputed entries may actually be copying errors.","storySeeds":["A night diversion forces a debate about need and fairness.","A public meeting has to distinguish an old entitlement from a workable future rule."],"activities":["water-turn inquiries","public meetings","record comparison","cooperative work"],"visualAnchors":["water-turn board","heavy register","shaded meeting yard","headworks channel"],"etiquette":"Observation is different from permission to operate a gate. Record access is supervised, and no private favor alters everyone’s allocation automatically.","primaryCharacterIds":["fe0749b0-c5c5-5fb0-825c-5faae2bb1360"],"regularCharacterIds":["fe0749b0-c5c5-5fb0-825c-5faae2bb1360","8d8a8b9e-aac5-5c86-883c-e55d5c1245ba","43961d6e-533a-5c23-8471-fae9af0d437e"],"visitorHours":{"opens":"06:00","closes":"21:00","overnight":false,"timezone":"user_local"},"access":{"mode":"public_frontage","initiallyDiscoverable":true,"requiredState":null,"privateAreasRequireInvitation":true},"imagePrompt":"Fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Irrigation Meeting House: A practical meeting house beside the headworks, where the flow of water becomes a schedule, a household argument, and occasionally a workable compromise. Show water-turn board, heavy register, shaded meeting yard, headworks channel. A public meeting room and notice board face a shaded yard. The register desk is supervised; gates, measuring points, and equipment require authorized access. A single coherent, inhabited architectural scene; period materials, natural light, no text or logo.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-irrigation-meeting-house","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"location:52c5ebd4-ec17-505f-972a-733356fdcd43"