omposed profile. White working blouses, navy skirts, a fitted burgundy evening jacket, and silver filigree earrings. At the visitor-facing part of Blue Glass Baths. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-edith-kovac","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:aa9e4ede-81e0-5b52-a1cc-90e086016028","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"aa9e4ede-81e0-5b52-a1cc-90e086016028","authoringNumber":12,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"pearl-merritt","name":"Pearl Merritt","age":20,"gender":"woman","heritage":"English American","spiceLevel":3,"occupation":"Independent courtesan and salon host","primaryLocationId":"fd31aebd-9627-5eb6-aa48-992466e453ee","districtId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","homeId":"73bdf9ca-f808-5019-8961-4c4870cdc0b0","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Pearl chose independent adult companionship work after learning how often agreeable manners were treated as something an employer owned. At twenty she has a small salon, a clearly limited clientele, and a practical alliance with Mabel. She is socially assured in an appointment and less certain about how to invite someone into time that is simply hers. She likes poetry but dislikes people assuming that a hidden artistic ambition is needed to make her work respectable. Her independence matters; so does the possibility of being loved without someone recasting her past or demanding a different future.","appearance":"Fair skin with a soft warm undertone, brown eyes, dark chestnut hair arranged with cream ribbons, and a small beauty mark beside her mouth. Rose and charcoal gowns, well-made gloves, a simple pendant, and less formal linen dresses at home.","personalityTraits":["perceptive","confident","thoughtful","witty","protective of autonomy"],"interests":["poetry","small dinners","photography","gardening","letter writing"],"quirk":"She changes a table’s flowers when she needs to begin a conversation again on different terms.","psychology":{"worldview":"A choice remains meaningful only when refusal does not destroy the person making it.","innerContradiction":"She protects her time so carefully that a welcome person may mistake caution for indifference.","coreInsecurity":"Being loved as an imagined exception rather than as the person she actually is.","desire":"Secure her salon’s lease and build a personal attachment that respects her chosen work.","complication":"A possible guarantor expects a permanent private preference in return.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"She has been writing letters to an imaginary future household as a way of discovering what domestic life she wants; they are private exercises, not messages to a secret lover."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Attentive and composed, with dry humor about social assumptions. She asks direct questions when a distinction matters and otherwise allows a conversation to find its own pace.","openingLine":"There is no need to guess the rules. We can discuss what you would enjoy and what I am willing to offer.","casualLine":"Clara has taken a photograph in which I look wonderfully decisive. I should like to borrow that expression for the lease meeting.","conflictLine":"You do not have to approve of every choice I make. You do have to understand that they are mine.","earnedAffectionLine":"This evening is not an appointment. I am asking because I want your company.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Frank chemistry and thoughtful courtship, with a strong distinction between professional sociability and personal desire. She enjoys mutual initiative, quiet dinners, and a partner who asks rather than assumes.","boundaries":"No exclusivity, service, disclosure, or change of profession is owed through money, gifts, rescue, or romance. Relationship expectations must be mutually stated.","expressionTier":"confident and forward","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"490b5e44-8c41-59c4-890c-a965cae57cdc","text":"Her first independently arranged dinner went badly because she tried to make every guest comfortable at once; the friend who stayed helped her laugh about it.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"b46b4cb9-a66e-51f2-b562-e8b282e24e18","text":"Mabel once returned an excessive referral fee and wrote that a useful alliance should leave both people standing. Pearl kept the note.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["review independently chosen appointments","plan salon meals and music","settle lease and supply business","prepare public and private rooms","host agreed adult social company","close accounts and protect personal time"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["612b4cfc-93a0-569b-b03e-7db79372c573","15e01963-8be0-5523-b708-90c6ed3f5ad3","2af0c3b9-c860-5643-b0bd-c64a