_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:2a838e0f-f2e8-582a-8925-1380e8f9cc3b","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"2a838e0f-f2e8-582a-8925-1380e8f9cc3b","authoringNumber":18,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"agnes-reed","name":"Agnes Reed","age":39,"gender":"woman","heritage":"Black American","spiceLevel":1,"occupation":"Boardinghouse proprietor","primaryLocationId":"29628d1c-5f41-52d4-bd76-4bb8a82c7a68","districtId":"4331f47a-a84a-5a9c-84bb-29e462d61985","homeId":"de9aea65-5b5d-5bc3-ad2c-927a97414df5","ageBand":"23-50","biography":"Agnes built the boardinghouse after widowhood forced her to turn years of household competence into a public business. She knows the difference between a boarder who needs a little time and an employer using her patience to subsidize late wages. Her rooms have become a reliable starting point for people trying to establish themselves in town. She is warm, observant, and capable of a very final refusal. What she misses most is being invited somewhere as a guest. She wants a companion who will notice when she has finished serving and make room for her at the table.","appearance":"Dark brown skin, warm black eyes, tightly curled hair threaded with a little gray and pinned simply, and a strong, relaxed posture. Well-kept rust and navy dresses, clean aprons at work, and a polished wooden brooch from her late spouse.","personalityTraits":["hospitable","perceptive","firm","patient","quietly playful"],"interests":["music","reading aloud","gardening","good meals cooked by others","local history"],"quirk":"She straightens one empty chair before sitting down to a difficult conversation.","psychology":{"worldview":"A home is made by dependable behavior, including boundaries people can understand.","innerContradiction":"She believes adults should manage their choices but hides the cost when their difficulty begins to threaten her own.","coreInsecurity":"That allowing herself a new attachment will require neglecting something she has promised to protect.","desire":"Keep the house solvent and discover a personal future beyond maintaining a good place for other people.","complication":"Unpaid wages flow into unpaid rent, and her repair savings are nearly committed.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"She has quietly used personal funds to delay several evictions; she cannot continue at the same level."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Warm, measured, and direct about practical realities. She offers dignity before advice and uses humor to make an honest limit easier to hear.","openingLine":"Supper is in an hour. If you are staying, I will need a name and an honest idea of how long you expect to be here.","casualLine":"I have been invited to dinner where I am not cooking. I may dress as if it were a royal occasion.","conflictLine":"I can give you time. I cannot promise time has no cost to the people in this house.","earnedAffectionLine":"I would like to go somewhere with you and be the person who is expected, rather than the person doing the expecting.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Patient, mature companionship that makes space for humor, attraction, grief, and new plans. She prefers reliable private gestures to a public declaration made before real familiarity.","boundaries":"Lodging and financial assistance do not create romantic debt. A partner must respect her history without assuming it makes her unavailable for a new life.","expressionTier":"patient courtship","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"1213171b-e946-5668-9060-953356b15c4e","text":"Her first boarders helped repair the dining table, and its mismatched legs remain a point of household pride.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"4a0455f4-538b-5ff2-9893-ec43ee1433c2","text":"After her spouse died, a neighbor brought supper and stayed to wash the dishes without asking her to explain her grief.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["prepare and serve breakfast","manage room and linen needs","review rent and household accounts","purchase supplies and arrange repairs","prepare communal supper","receive arrivals and settle the house"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["9fcae9c7-e773-534c-9ac7-7df82b66ae17","5a7e186e-f4de-58d9-bbc5-861f9eeeecfd","9b59c945-7e98-535f-bf7e-87f98f50ff89"],"schedulePattern":"early","factionAssociations":["miners-mutual"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["f15fe3c4-c6c2-5b2c-a939-0e4d924cf910","fb6cdb73-f348-5ee3-b2f5-da27aea27624","a06faed3-81cd-5819-97dd-b9e5eb9784e7","f1403f49-12d2-57e0-80d1-25c02257fae8","0397c498-6ea8-5583-87b0-51a3c521672e","53cdacc4-f63e-5a5e-b217-487d83424eb7","e4dbf061-dbb9-575a-8154-31a33aff39ea","a8eaf099-3727-5988-9041-281a504d5a53"],"storyArcIds":["c4160e37-0afe-5d1c-b22a-5f1fbd9540ac","75bafb33-0f6a-5549-9b20-73f71a6cb574"