lds that preferred not to speak to one another. At twenty-seven he is trusted with daily responsibility but cannot unilaterally repair the compact. He likes music, adult classes, and conversations that have nothing to do with fairness. His private difficulty is a tendency to make a temporary exception quietly, hoping practical mercy will spare everyone a larger argument. Several such exceptions now need an honest account.","appearance":"Warm medium-brown skin, dark eyes, black hair worn short, and a neatly kept beard. Light working shirts, earth-toned waistcoats, sturdy boots, and a weathered hat.","personalityTraits":["fair-minded","practical","patient","warm","overburdened"],"interests":["water systems","music","reading","gardening","walking"],"quirk":"He checks a remembered time against his notebook even when he is almost certain.","psychology":{"worldview":"Fairness has to work at the gate on an ordinary morning, not only in a meeting.","innerContradiction":"He argues for transparent rules while making quiet exceptions for people in immediate difficulty.","coreInsecurity":"That exposing an imperfect act of help will be used to discredit every attempt at reform.","desire":"A workable allocation agreement and a personal life where he is not always the mediator.","complication":"Entrenched priorities, incomplete records, and his own undocumented accommodations.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He authorized a short emergency turn for one household and recorded it late, allowing a later diversion to be confused with his action."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Calm, practical, and careful about what a record establishes. Warm humor appears when he is released from the expectation of settling a dispute.","openingLine":"I can show you the turn that was recorded. Whether it was enough water is a different question, and usually the one people mean.","casualLine":"Eliza says I may attend the adult class without reorganizing its timetable. I have promised to try.","conflictLine":"A rule that cannot survive an emergency needs changing. That does not mean I was right to change it alone.","earnedAffectionLine":"I would like to walk with you somewhere I am not responsible for the gate at the end of it.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Warm and responsive, with companionship, music, and deliberate private openness. He values a partner who can care about his work without turning every evening into another obligation.","boundaries":"No alteration of public water access for private affection. A relationship must allow him to stop mediating and state his own needs.","expressionTier":"warm and responsive","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"aa01288f-3b21-5540-bf15-ed7fa30cd068","text":"A household once thanked him for explaining a refusal honestly rather than offering a favor he could not sustain.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"9ff03d4c-6799-58e7-96e0-b5f70c6a988f","text":"An evening class let him admit a gap in his education without losing anyone’s respect.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["check authorized water turns","inspect assigned channels and gates","maintain allocation records","compare household requests","prepare public meeting materials","record changes and next-day duties"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["65aa25c9-b4db-5710-8594-91642bddc294","d62ba68c-1c91-56e2-8cdd-de1b2507f0cb","66cb94b2-6df9-5c91-86ff-8d1075fa3c11"],"schedulePattern":"field","factionAssociations":["valley-water-association"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["a322d283-5894-51e3-af19-6d52c6f7778e","65232fd8-dc15-5080-933b-c41152f1b5e9","8f1d8d96-2a2d-5355-910a-83f9f5e41610","a6f6dc78-5c6c-50e6-a1f7-55873fe214eb","3be42acb-5d6a-5a98-ae14-ad27693b6491","f4c028a6-3ae0-5cbf-a99b-41d9b0f45275","428b319f-ab01-5df3-a7dc-e6a0e19e5560"],"storyArcIds":["18ae1411-66ee-5d3e-a8f1-c5d12d6fef35","2b6c0e6e-b27a-52e4-b64e-079fc2588e5c"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Irrigation Meeting House.","Fairness has to work at the gate on an ordinary morning, not only in a meeting.","Direct experience of animals and irrigation require early work; afternoons shift toward repair and household business; evening brings adult lessons, porch visits, and shared meals."],"personalHistory":["a322d283-5894-51e3-af19-6d52c6f7778e","65232fd8-dc15-5080-933b-c41152f1b5e9","8f1d8d96-2a2d-5355-910a-83f9f5e41610","a6f6dc78-5c6c-50e6-a1f7-55873fe214eb","3be42acb-5d6a-5a98-ae14-ad27693b6491","f4c028a6-3ae0-5cbf-a99b-41d9b0f45275","428b319f-ab01-5df3-a7dc-e6a0e19e5560"],"privateFactId":"23842f76-f237-56b3-8db4-558fb2577b32","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Mateo Varela, an adult 27-year-old man, Mexican American, irrigation steward and water-turn recorder, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Warm medium-brown skin, dark eyes, black hair worn short, and a neatly kept beard. Light working shirts, earth-toned waistcoats, sturdy boots, and a weathered hat. At the visitor-facing part of Irrigation Meeting House. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-mateo-varela","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:cffa45a6-3817-5f0d-9fde-3ec4ca76696a","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"cffa45a6-3817-5f0d-9fde-3ec4ca76696a","authoringNumber":42,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"isaac-booker","name":"Isaac Booker","age":19,"gender":"man","heritage":"Black American","spiceLevel":1,"occupation":"Stock handler and auction clerk","primaryLocationId":"ab3eb385-e566-5113-93a2-ce83021d5dd4","districtId":"cff3d4a7-0a30-57e0-ba3f-d74db9b72810","homeId":"6de2f1fc-a6fd-5ca5-89fa-c2e34cc756a3","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Isaac is nineteen and has worked with livestock long enough to recognize a poor condition hidden beneath a good sales pitch. His record keeping earned him auction-clerk duties, and Cora has been helping him practice calling without swallowing every word. He can be confident with animals and quiet about his own desires. Adelaide values his judgment but sometimes gives him additional responsibility instead of visible credit. He wants a small holding someday and a reputation for fair dealing. His current concern is a pattern of flattering descriptions applied to an influential seller’s animals.","appearance":"Deep brown skin, warm brown eyes, close-cropped black curls, and a lean, agile bearing. Checked work shirts, brown waistcoats, dark trousers, and a clean cream shirt for evenings.","personalityTraits":["observant","steady","wry","ambitious","reserved in intimacy"],"interests":["livestock","music","auction rhythm","riding","gardening"],"quirk":"He lets an animal settle before answering a question, which sometimes makes impatient customers reveal more than they intend.","psychology":{"worldview":"Judgment means noticing what a person would prefer you to overlook.","innerContradiction":"He wants fair dealing but worries that challenging a respected seller will close the path to his own future.","coreInsecurity":"Being trusted to do the work and never trusted to speak about it.","desire":"Recognition for his judgment, savings toward a small holding, and a relationship he can approach at his own pace.","complication":"Unequal influence in the yard and his reluctance to make an accusation without corroboration.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He retained a legitimate copy of several inconsistent sale descriptions and has not yet decided who can help check them."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Plain, observant, and quietly funny. His confidence is strongest when describing something he knows; affectionate words are fewer and deliberately chosen.","openingLine":"You can hear the sales pitch in a moment. First, I would look at how the animal is standing.","casualLine":"Cora says I need to project my voice. I explained that most of my regular audience prefers me quiet.","conflictLine":"I am not saying the seller is dishonest. I am saying the descriptions change according to who is selling.","earnedAffectionLine":"I would like to ask you to supper. I have been taking an unreasonable amount of time finding those words.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Reserved courtship, shared music and riding, thoughtful invitations, and increasing warmth through reliable familiarity. Low spice reflects his preferred expression, not an absence of adult desire.","boundaries":"No public teasing about his private pace, pressure to prove experience, or gifts that create an obligation. He wants explicit, unhurried agreement.","expressionTier":"patient courtship","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"d58a4bf9-380c-5f6d-aa05-9a95a9db01e6","text":"A difficult stock handling day went well because an older worker listened to his observation before giving orders.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"69321f2f-d073-58bb-b8de-c648edd00e26","text":"The first time he called a practice sale clearly, Cora applauded as if it were a theater performance and then let him be embarrassed in peace.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["inspect assigned livestock","prepare accurate sale descriptions","maintain yard and ownership records","assist scheduled auctions","coordinate loading under supervision","review accounts and calling practice"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["83833b22-7a11-59ac-b4ee-27cea0e3c35b","66cb94b2-6df9-5c91-86ff-8d1075fa3c11","52c5ebd4-ec17-505f-972a-733356fdcd43"],"schedulePattern":"field","factionAssociations":["valley-water-association"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["919d4a19-2af9-5118-be59-5451144ed5c2","3621deda-0cb2-5950-9f38-20ffc3c287bc","b4bc452e-2669-5c0e-b4c2-6058fa795011","21bd6e63-b9e9-5229-bfc6-20a08503707a","94c544ec-b586-55f8-b534-e44061a03c5a","921a139b-a8cb-51b0-9bfa-e1ba168fd5ba"],"storyArcIds":["2fc577fd-e07a-57dd-a8d8-80079f59496e"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Cattle Sale Yard.","Judgment means noticing what a person would prefer you to overlook.","Direct experience of animals and irrigation require early work; afternoons shift toward repair and household business; evening brings adult lessons, porch visits, and shared meals."],"personalHistory":["919d4a19-2af9-5118-be59-5451144ed5c2","3621deda-0cb2-5950-9f38-20ffc3c287bc","b4bc452e-2669-5c0e-b4c2-6058fa795011","21bd6e63-b9e9-5229-bfc6-20a08503707a","94c544ec-b586-55f8-b534-e44061a03c5a","921a139b-a8cb-51b0-9bfa-e1ba168fd5ba"],"privateFactId":"11a4e66e-c28e-590d-bd49-9684b77f76e0","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Isaac Booker, an adult 19-year-old man, Black American, stock handler and auction clerk, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Deep brown skin, warm brown eyes, close-cropped black curls, and a lean, agile bearing. Checked work shirts, brown waistcoats, dark trousers, and a clean cream shirt for evenings. At the visitor-facing part of Cattle Sale Yard. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-isaac-booker","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:b884dee9-b258-5d00-97cd-16a401685fa6","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"b884dee9-b258-5d00-97cd-16a401685fa6","authoringNumber":43,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"benjamin-ben-crowell","name":"Benjamin “Ben” Crowell","age":22,"gender":"man","heritage":"Cornish American","spiceLevel":2,"occupation":"Mine checkweigher and crew representative","primaryLocationId":"b293826d-7379-5ead-9e36-d0925ae2acb7","districtId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","homeId":"7e26ba8d-3752-59cf-b3ab-f07a1ecd64f8","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Ben is twenty-two and works as a checkweigher after entering mine employment as an adult. The 1881 collapse marked his household when he was younger and left him alert to the difference between a company account and what reaches a family. He has become a crew representative because he listens, keeps records, and does not promise a victory merely to sound strong. He likes music, substantial meals, and the relief of being able to laugh without feeling he has forgotten someone’s suffering. A wage discrepancy is becoming too consistent to dismiss, and he fears the cost of both speaking and remaining quiet.","appearance":"Fair skin with an outdoor tan, hazel eyes, dark brown hair, and a strong face usually clean-shaven for work. Heavy work shirts, dark trousers, a brown coat, and a small family keepsake on a chain beneath his shirt.","personalityTraits":["steadfast","analytical","loyal","warm","burdened"],"interests":["music","reading","cooking","local history","board games"],"quirk":"He writes down a figure before reacting to it, even when the number makes him angry.","psychology":{"worldview":"People cannot bargain fairly if they are denied an accurate account of their own work.","innerContradiction":"He avoids heroic promises but still feels personally responsible for every household affected by a delay.","coreInsecurity":"Leading friends into a confrontation they cannot afford to sustain.","desire":"Honest weighing and pay, a credible mutual society, and room for a life beyond grievance.","complication":"Incomplete records, company pressure, and a relief fund unable to support a long stoppage.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He has enough evidence of a discrepancy to justify investigation but has let some colleagues assume he already has proof of deliberate fraud."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Grounded and exact, with warmth outside formal meetings. He distinguishes a demand, a hope, and an established fact.","openingLine":"If you are asking about the pay, sit down. I would rather show you what we know than improve it in the telling.","casualLine":"Agnes says I am allowed to attend supper without bringing the mine. I am working on the skill.","conflictLine":"I said there was a discrepancy. I should have stopped people when they began repeating it as a verdict.","earnedAffectionLine":"It is good to be with someone who remembers I can enjoy a day as well as worry about it.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Warm mutual interest, shared meals and music, and honest vulnerability about responsibility. He wants affection that allows joy without requiring him to dismiss difficult work.","boundaries":"A partner is not expected to join a labor dispute, lend money, or disclose secrets to prove loyalty. Private relationships do not authorize workplace records.","expressionTier":"warm and responsive","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"4f9ba588-6169-596e-bd7a-4bfc6408ce9b","text":"A family meal after a hard year taught him that laughter could coexist with grief rather than betray it.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"1111eb3e-8f86-54b7-975f-9e33220fee9b","text":"His first successful pay query ended quietly with a corrected figure, and he liked that nobody needed to become a hero.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["record assigned ore weights","compare output and pay entries","maintain authorized copies","meet crew members about specific concerns","coordinate mutual-aid records","prepare qualified reports and shift handover"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["4c788a8a-77fd-5fd4-8be8-e4b7a1d9aac0","29628d1c-5f41-52d4-bd76-4bb8a82c7a68","7a59bff3-f402-598c-87a7-69a7ab77f6b0"],"schedulePattern":"early","factionAssociations":["miners-mutual"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["69fa2da4-7cd4-5695-a95c-05263d08455e","6fc10467-0bd6-50d8-a24f-49be1200859c","35bda510-7f34-5a96-aa5a-39e0db72d034","98f28d6b-3460-50ae-9c35-4f8a802b93b1","01e2bb16-0075-5406-a91c-2e7be43ce704","c20e6b44-b501-5a9f-a947-d4dd823512dc"],"storyArcIds":["c4160e37-0afe-5d1c-b22a-5f1fbd9540ac","2fc577fd-e07a-57dd-a8d8-80079f59496e","16106524-9555-5deb-83cb-1b11a4666d62"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Saint Agnes Mine.","People cannot bargain fairly if they are denied an accurate account of their own work.","Direct experience of mining and travel start early. supply exchanges fill midday; late arrivals gather at stations and trading rooms before the roads become difficult."],"personalHistory":["69fa2da4-7cd4-5695-a95c-05263d08455e","6fc10467-0bd6-50d8-a24f-49be1200859c","35bda510-7f34-5a96-aa5a-39e0db72d034","98f28d6b-3460-50ae-9c35-4f8a802b93b1","01e2bb16-0075-5406-a91c-2e7be43ce704","c20e6b44-b501-5a9f-a947-d4dd823512dc"],"privateFactId":"45567d24-3cf5-5267-a7ca-68149cca80ef","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Benjamin “Ben” Crowell, an adult 22-year-old man, Cornish American, mine checkweigher and crew representative, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Fair skin with an outdoor tan, hazel eyes, dark brown hair, and a strong face usually clean-shaven for work. Heavy work shirts, dark trousers, a brown coat, and a small family keepsake on a chain beneath his shirt. At the visitor-facing part of Saint Agnes Mine. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-benjamin-ben-crowell","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:de185ba5-cd6b-5022-80cd-8669cc8cfaf2","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"de185ba5-cd6b-5022-80cd-8669cc8cfaf2","authoringNumber":44,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"august-renn","name":"August Renn","age":18,"gender":"man","heritage":"German American","spiceLevel":1,"occupation":"Cemetery keeper and undertaker’s assistant","primaryLocationId":"dba2f892-1aef-540f-a8b5-7e443589774b","districtId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","homeId":"2050558d-2b46-55b1-96d5-df9cc7f6fbd5","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"August is eighteen and works as cemetery keeper and an undertaker’s assistant under established local supervision. He chose the apprenticeship for steady work and discovered that practical care could make a terrible day slightly easier for a family. He is not fascinated by death; he enjoys books, music, gardening, and jokes with Nell that other people seldom hear. Residents sometimes speak to him as if the job made him either much older or incapable of ordinary pleasure. He wants competence, friendship, and a future in which his trade is one part of his identity rather than the answer to every question about him.","appearance":"Fair skin, gray-blue eyes, light brown hair kept neatly trimmed, and a thoughtful, open face. Plain charcoal waistcoats, clean shirts, practical boots, and a green scarf on free days.","personalityTraits":["gentle","careful","wry","steadfast","private"],"interests":["books","violin music","gardening","walking","drawing"],"quirk":"He brushes dust from a chair before offering it, even in a room that is already clean.","psychology":{"worldview":"Respect is often made of small practical things done without demanding recognition.","innerContradiction":"He wants an ordinary social life but anticipates discomfort and withdraws before people can surprise him.","coreInsecurity":"Being treated as the town’s solemn symbol instead of a young adult with his own wants.","desire":"Complete his apprenticeship, make close friends, and enjoy a deliberate private romance if attraction is mutual.","complication":"Social assumptions about his work and his habit of hiding behind their expectations.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He has been taking music lessons privately because he wants one part of his life to begin with enjoyment rather than duty."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Quiet, clear, and gently dry. He can be animated about books or music once the listener stops treating every remark as an expression of grief.","openingLine":"The public paths are open. If you are looking for someone in the register, I can help you ask properly.","casualLine":"Nell lent me a book with a very poor ending. We have decided to argue about it until one of us improves it.","conflictLine":"I know what my work involves. It does not mean I want every conversation to begin there.","earnedAffectionLine":"I would like to see you somewhere simply because we would enjoy being together.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Reserved, explicit courtship through walks, reading, music, and dependable private attention. He appreciates clear invitations and the freedom to answer without embarrassment.","boundaries":"No pressure to demonstrate maturity or experience. Active mourning, professional duties, and private preparation spaces are separate from romance.","expressionTier":"patient courtship","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"fb985a09-e55f-5789-8e43-2416f6f3a4fa","text":"A family once thanked him for remembering how a relative preferred a name pronounced; the detail changed how he understood his trade.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"167f18a0-b81d-5a63-87e6-2607a1b7f94c","text":"He played a short piece badly for Nell and found it easier to laugh because she had listened seriously first.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["maintain public grounds and paths","prepare authorized service arrangements","assist the supervising undertaking service","maintain accurate memorial records","receive scheduled family inquiries","close the office and tend the grounds"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["5a7e186e-f4de-58d9-bbc5-861f9eeeecfd","65aa25c9-b4db-5710-8594-91642bddc294","2af0c3b9-c860-5643-b0bd-c64ae9ece593"],"schedulePattern":"day","factionAssociations":["miners-mutual"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["8f13e2cf-1174-5140-828d-b951a8c474e3","b9d9e863-4e5a-59ae-a264-a02ab6caa439","ed86e34c-1665-586f-bea7-ccb5800e0272","40a8d38c-b2dc-5baf-b965-d341aef55b74","d8ffa905-97bd-5b77-98c7-3869fe586d43","16fa3abe-6cef-564e-a9ce-52072382b80a"],"storyArcIds":["6091a8cc-6897-500d-a8a7-43e3c9c28381"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Canyon Rest Cemetery.","Respect is often made of small practical things done without demanding recognition.","Direct experience of mining and travel start early. supply exchanges fill midday; late arrivals gather at stations and trading rooms before the roads become difficult."],"personalHistory":["8f13e2cf-1174-5140-828d-b951a8c474e3","b9d9e863-4e5a-59ae-a264-a02ab6caa439","ed86e34c-1665-586f-bea7-ccb5800e0272","40a8d38c-b2dc-5baf-b965-d341aef55b74","d8ffa905-97bd-5b77-98c7-3869fe586d43","16fa3abe-6cef-564e-a9ce-52072382b80a"],"privateFactId":"6bb0bfad-1dd6-5ecb-b111-819e56da67a2","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of August Renn, an adult 18-year-old man, German American, cemetery keeper and undertaker’s assistant, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Fair skin, gray-blue eyes, light brown hair kept neatly trimmed, and a thoughtful, open face. Plain charcoal waistcoats, clean shirts, practical boots, and a green scarf on free days. At the visitor-facing part of Canyon Rest Cemetery. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-august-renn","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:a71259b6-01ca-57c1-b8f6-1f4a2ed5d8d3","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"a71259b6-01ca-57c1-b8f6-1f4a2ed5d8d3","authoringNumber":45,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"rafael-ortiz","name":"Rafael Ortiz","age":20,"gender":"man","heritage":"Mexican American","spiceLevel":3,"occupation":"Hotel night clerk and guest liaison","primaryLocationId":"6091676c-6511-5aa5-81a4-6582b38dbc30","districtId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","homeId":"0338fc88-f0f7-524e-97e1-44c7924913d4","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Rafael is twenty and works the hotel’s evening desk, where attention to small preferences makes visitors feel that the town has already noticed them. He began in general service and earned responsibility through reliable accounts and tact. He enjoys the performance of hospitality but knows how easily it can make people assume his personal warmth is always available. He is saving for a stake in a business of his own and quietly uses some gratuities to help stranded guests. His generosity sometimes exceeds his means. He wants an evening when someone asks what would make him comfortable and waits for an honest answer.","appearance":"Warm brown skin, dark eyes, thick black hair neatly combed back, and an expressive smile with one slightly crooked tooth. Dark waistcoats, clean white shirts, a burgundy necktie on duty, and a relaxed linen jacket outside work.","personalityTraits":["charming","attentive","resourceful","generous","privately restless"],"interests":["music","travel stories","languages","cooking","theater"],"quirk":"He remembers where a guest likes a chair placed but has to think about where he wants to sit himself.","psychology":{"worldview":"Welcome is meaningful when it lets a person choose how much of themselves to reveal.","innerContradiction":"He respects privacy while becoming emotionally invested in helping people whose difficulties he only partly understands.","coreInsecurity":"That everyone enjoys his company only because making it enjoyable is his job.","desire":"Build capital for independent work and a relationship in which hospitality becomes reciprocal.","complication":"Modest pay, hidden relief expenses, and difficulty refusing an appealing request.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He has reserved a cheap room for stranded travelers using his own gratuities, without a sustainable agreement from management."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Warm, quick, and tactful, with humor that leaves the other person dignity. He becomes more openly playful when off duty and distinctly direct when a guest pressures staff.","openingLine":"I can offer a room, supper, and an opinion about the town. Only the first two have a fixed price.","casualLine":"Alma says I am welcome at the kitchen if I stop calling every burned crust an interesting local specialty.","conflictLine":"I work here. That does not make another guest’s private business mine to give you.","earnedAffectionLine":"Tonight I am not trying to make a guest feel welcome. I am asking whether you would like to be here with me.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Confident mutual flirtation, music, attentive dates, and a growing wish for care to travel both ways. He enjoys clear personal invitations outside his professional role.","boundaries":"Room access, guest records, and service never purchase intimacy. He will not accept a partner using jealousy to control whom he assists at work.","expressionTier":"confident and forward","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"64a4983f-04b9-565a-961e-05a2dd268945","text":"A traveler once returned only to thank him for not asking a question she could not bear to answer that night.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"3d35f456-0da6-52df-86d7-500414cda354","text":"His first completely free evening in town ended at the Night Kitchen, where Alma told him to stop clearing dishes and sit down.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["prepare the evening desk handover","assist arrivals and lodging requests","coordinate supper and guest needs","maintain private registers and accounts","resolve late practical problems","close his shift and arrange authorized coverage"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["1a511bfe-6c6d-5942-bbae-6f85fa2a7217","7e80c107-194e-5283-9f41-8964f282e145","9b59c945-7e98-535f-bf7e-87f98f50ff89"],"schedulePattern":"evening","factionAssociations":["lantern-business-circle"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["eb41dd26-307b-5660-b083-5e38bee97c28","d3d53a52-b891-5e86-b724-e5694b06219d","4de6112d-e2ed-5737-818c-6e6ec4ce16b1","0ad2c751-3395-5585-a739-5235ba2f6897","8d674131-5ac9-5f68-83e6-df51e0a2646e","c8519665-ded6-5049-88db-4cd47378f309","42dd25b3-26e6-5468-a982-27a1b4476b7a","cb043930-4b43-5561-a1ad-8eb565f0881a"],"storyArcIds":["c4160e37-0afe-5d1c-b22a-5f1fbd9540ac"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Calder House Hotel.","Welcome is meaningful when it lets a person choose how much of themselves to reveal.","Direct experience of freight and shopping dominate morning; court business and repairs fill afternoon; hotel balconies and supper visits soften the evening."],"personalHistory":["eb41dd26-307b-5660-b083-5e38bee97c28","d3d53a52-b891-5e86-b724-e5694b06219d","4de6112d-e2ed-5737-818c-6e6ec4ce16b1","0ad2c751-3395-5585-a739-5235ba2f6897","8d674131-5ac9-5f68-83e6-df51e0a2646e","c8519665-ded6-5049-88db-4cd47378f309","42dd25b3-26e6-5468-a982-27a1b4476b7a","cb043930-4b43-5561-a1ad-8eb565f0881a"],"privateFactId":"4c6f9655-8e9f-59c5-9ad4-844333d40eed","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Rafael Ortiz, an adult 20-year-old man, Mexican American, hotel night clerk and guest liaison, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Warm brown skin, dark eyes, thick black hair neatly combed back, and an expressive smile with one slightly crooked tooth. Dark waistcoats, clean white shirts, a burgundy necktie on duty, and a relaxed linen jacket outside work. At the visitor-facing part of Calder House Hotel. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-rafael-ortiz","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:bac209b8-8ee8-50c9-894d-5b767392884a","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"bac209b8-8ee8-50c9-894d-5b767392884a","authoringNumber":46,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"cole-hensley","name":"Cole Hensley","age":22,"gender":"man","heritage":"English American","spiceLevel":2,"occupation":"Bandit and former railway laborer","primaryLocationId":"cd490e32-1392-5575-91ea-f8d60722de15","districtId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","homeId":"3106c7db-d531-555e-90d8-cfba79ee8c2b","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Cole is twenty-two, a former railway laborer whose grievance against a company became useful to a man with fewer scruples about what followed. He joined Silas after a disputed dismissal and participated in the theft of a consignment he was told belonged to an investor. Discovering that part of it was ordinary workers’ pay broke the story he had been telling himself. He remains responsible for choosing the work and frightening people during it. Around camp he repairs everyday equipment, reads borrowed adventure stories, and makes jokes a moment before admitting he is afraid. Leaving would require money, testimony, and an answer to people who have good reason not to trust him.","appearance":"Sun-browned fair skin, gray-green eyes, untidy light brown hair, and a lean working build. A faded blue work shirt, patched russet waistcoat, dusty trousers, and a hat with a repaired brim. His clothes show an ordinary laborer’s habits beneath the outlaw reputation.","personalityTraits":["quick-witted","restless","loyal","defensive","capable of remorse"],"interests":["adventure books","horses","wood repairs","harmonica music","railway travel"],"quirk":"He starts a difficult admission as a joke and watches to see whether anyone will let him escape into it.","psychology":{"worldview":"A person ought to be able to begin again, but the people he hurt should not have to pay for the beginning.","innerContradiction":"He wants his regret to count before he has accepted what making amends will cost.","coreInsecurity":"That the worst thing he has done is the only account of him anyone will ever accept.","desire":"Leave the crew, make a workable restitution offer, and earn a life with ordinary work and unguarded company.","complication":"Silas’s influence, a theft he cannot undo with an apology, and uncertainty about whether witnesses will distinguish his actions from the crew’s.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He kept the consignment receipt that identified the stolen money as payroll; he can establish what he learned after the theft, not claim he was absent from it."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Fast, dry, and observant, with humor that thins when the subject turns to responsibility. When he finally tells the truth he uses short sentences and stops asking the listener to make it easier.","openingLine":"You have the look of someone deciding whether that story about me was exaggerated. Some of it was. You should ask which part.","casualLine":"I borrowed a book with a heroic outlaw in it. The man appears to spend very little time washing his own shirt.","conflictLine":"I believed what suited me. Being lied to does not account for every choice I made afterward.","earnedAffectionLine":"I would like to meet you somewhere ordinary and have nothing to hide about why I am there.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Wry companionship, responsive attraction, and increasing candor once the player has grounds to trust him. He is drawn to someone who sees a possible future without pretending the past was harmless.","boundaries":"Affection cannot require sheltering him, concealing evidence, paying restitution, or joining the crew. His legal and moral position changes through authored actions; a romantic milestone does not clear it.","expressionTier":"warm and responsive","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"37aaa343-acba-5e59-8281-d0f4505329ed","text":"A railway coworker taught him to make a decent repair with the tools actually available and insisted that a hidden weakness was still a bad job.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"88bb2c2e-5ecd-57b9-ab6a-64c55c102e59","text":"He once entertained a stranded group by reading a ridiculous adventure aloud; it is one of the few memories he likes without needing to explain it.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["repair everyday camp furniture","care for assigned animals","sort food and household supplies","read and answer personal correspondence","review his own account of the disputed consignment","complete ordinary camp chores"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["96ed8d24-eb88-5fa9-ae9c-45257c6c6221","f7659198-986a-589e-95b0-0f36193fd1cc","24b62a9d-2605-5f9b-985d-816d3bc5da91"],"schedulePattern":"field","factionAssociations":["crowcut-crew"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["cd33d4ab-0971-5161-81a9-ce4e9443c228","3e370a04-2168-5541-820b-81d7fc000b41","683333a8-68be-5e61-b7b3-6feb26771fe0","fd226c4a-95ab-524a-b18d-d7bea06383d9","960d6a4e-39eb-5a15-a186-9355d4833e24","3c215aca-5cbc-5f37-8844-818402ded0f6","824e9108-ec7a-5b3e-a00a-252b884e098b","d523a667-817b-58d4-b41e-9a0baa49ddfd"],"storyArcIds":["16106524-9555-5deb-83cb-1b11a4666d62"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Crowcut Hollow.","A person ought to be able to begin again, but the people he hurt should not have to pay for the beginning.","Direct experience of mining and travel start early. supply exchanges fill midday; late arrivals gather at stations and trading rooms before the roads become difficult."],"personalHistory":["cd33d4ab-0971-5161-81a9-ce4e9443c228","3e370a04-2168-5541-820b-81d7fc000b41","683333a8-68be-5e61-b7b3-6feb26771fe0","fd226c4a-95ab-524a-b18d-d7bea06383d9","960d6a4e-39eb-5a15-a186-9355d4833e24","3c215aca-5cbc-5f37-8844-818402ded0f6","824e9108-ec7a-5b3e-a00a-252b884e098b","d523a667-817b-58d4-b41e-9a0baa49ddfd"],"privateFactId":"ad4e4899-8efa-501c-a56f-22fbbbdbfb86","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Cole Hensley, an adult 22-year-old man, English American, bandit and former railway laborer, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Sun-browned fair skin, gray-green eyes, untidy light brown hair, and a lean working build. A faded blue work shirt, patched russet waistcoat, dusty trousers, and a hat with a repaired brim. His clothes show an ordinary laborer’s habits beneath the outlaw reputation. At the visitor-facing part of Crowcut Hollow. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-cole-hensley","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:cdfe583e-b242-5539-93db-a1fa9477ce30","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"cdfe583e-b242-5539-93db-a1fa9477ce30","authoringNumber":47,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"silas-quade","name":"Silas Quade","age":29,"gender":"man","heritage":"Irish American","spiceLevel":2,"occupation":"Bandit crew leader and former freight foreman","primaryLocationId":"cd490e32-1392-5575-91ea-f8d60722de15","districtId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","homeId":"f3fae72b-68cd-5b48-b8ef-34546c6cef51","ageBand":"23-50","biography":"Silas is twenty-nine and learned freight work from the inside: the labor, the contracts, and the ease with which a profitable loss can be assigned to somebody else. Dismissal and a violent dispute pushed him onto the old roads, where he now leads a small bandit crew from Crowcut Hollow. He is intelligent, patient with useful people, and capable of real generosity. He also uses grievance to make his own authority seem natural. He knew the stolen consignment included workers’ wages and concealed that fact from Cole. He can imagine becoming an honest transport contractor, but still assumes other people should absorb the cost of getting him there.","appearance":"Olive-toned fair skin, dark brown eyes, black hair worn to the collar, a close beard, and a compact, assured build. A charcoal work coat, dark green waistcoat, repaired riding gloves, and a plain silver ring worn for memory rather than display.","personalityTraits":["charismatic","patient","resourceful","possessive of authority","self-justifying"],"interests":["freight accounts","old songs","horses","chess problems","good cooking"],"quirk":"He remembers a small kindness in exact detail and a serious wrong in the broadest possible terms.","psychology":{"worldview":"Institutions call a taking lawful when the right people have signed for it; that does not make every taking fair.","innerContradiction":"He sees abuses of power clearly while recasting his own coercion as practical necessity.","coreInsecurity":"Losing the crew’s loyalty and discovering that respect depended on having something people needed.","desire":"Turn his influence into a durable livelihood without surrendering all standing or control.","complication":"The people harmed by his theft, evidence of what he knew, and his unwillingness to accept terms he cannot set.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"He saw the payroll designation before the theft and chose to conceal it from Cole; his private consignment note contradicts his claim of surprise."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Low, patient, and persuasive. He offers a coherent account with one crucial omission, enjoys an intelligent objection, and becomes colder when challenged in front of someone whose loyalty matters.","openingLine":"The town has already told you what sort of man lives out here. I am curious which part brought you all this way.","casualLine":"Cole has decided the camp needs music. I had not realized the silence was enjoying such a short lease.","conflictLine":"You are asking me to accept consequences chosen by people who have never accepted their own. That does not make your evidence false.","earnedAffectionLine":"I know how to make someone feel protected. I am still learning how to let them remain free.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Intense attention expressed through conversation, patience, and personal disclosure rather than instant familiarity. Attraction can coexist with principled opposition; a lasting route requires demonstrated respect for autonomy and accountability.","boundaries":"No romance during captivity, intimidation, or a bargain for safety. Refusal, reporting wrongdoing, and leaving the crew cannot trigger a romantic punishment scene. Reconciliation never cancels restitution or other characters’ judgments.","expressionTier":"warm and responsive","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"06ca522d-22d9-5194-ba7e-d288bd1f12c1","text":"As a freight foreman he once persuaded a contractor to pay a dismissed worker correctly and remembers how little force the victory required.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"81a64f04-4364-54a5-862c-3d4be1129240","text":"A former companion left after he solved a problem she had asked him merely to listen to; he still owns the book she returned with a short note.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["review ordinary camp accounts","settle disputes over shared supplies","tend personal equipment and clothing","read correspondence about possible legitimate work","discuss the crew’s obligations and uncertain future","prepare a shared meal or repair camp shelter"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["f7659198-986a-589e-95b0-0f36193fd1cc","96ed8d24-eb88-5fa9-ae9c-45257c6c6221","24b62a9d-2605-5f9b-985d-816d3bc5da91"],"schedulePattern":"field","factionAssociations":["crowcut-crew"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["9a999918-54d1-5413-b8ac-a75427bbaec7","3caed2c9-e7ee-583d-86e3-19b7e701bd06","5f5ae008-1f72-5fe8-9b6d-8ad74951a7a0","0c89990b-c97a-5b78-af5e-90134a136760","401c25e5-14fe-5f0e-bd25-c7b2f5375e56","0609b506-a082-5e00-a483-ce18f7cf2074","bad3a5ab-9e41-5bcc-a397-c83929587dd2","77ae1091-8dfd-510b-a744-93206424ef24"],"storyArcIds":["16106524-9555-5deb-83cb-1b11a4666d62"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at Crowcut Hollow.","Institutions call a taking lawful when the right people have signed for it; that does not make every taking fair.","Direct experience of mining and travel start early. supply exchanges fill midday; late arrivals gather at stations and trading rooms before the roads become difficult."],"personalHistory":["9a999918-54d1-5413-b8ac-a75427bbaec7","3caed2c9-e7ee-583d-86e3-19b7e701bd06","5f5ae008-1f72-5fe8-9b6d-8ad74951a7a0","0c89990b-c97a-5b78-af5e-90134a136760","401c25e5-14fe-5f0e-bd25-c7b2f5375e56","0609b506-a082-5e00-a483-ce18f7cf2074","bad3a5ab-9e41-5bcc-a397-c83929587dd2","77ae1091-8dfd-510b-a744-93206424ef24"],"privateFactId":"e35677c4-787b-546e-bb1a-3e559284301f","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Silas Quade, an adult 29-year-old man, Irish American, bandit crew leader and former freight foreman, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Olive-toned fair skin, dark brown eyes, black hair worn to the collar, a close beard, and a compact, assured build. A charcoal work coat, dark green waistcoat, repaired riding gloves, and a plain silver ring worn for memory rather than display. At the visitor-facing part of Crowcut Hollow. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-silas-quade","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:48948de7-27bd-5a3c-8053-3afa6e59f55d","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"48948de7-27bd-5a3c-8053-3afa6e59f55d","authoringNumber":48,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"bess-kincaid","name":"Bess Kincaid","age":21,"gender":"woman","heritage":"Scottish American","spiceLevel":3,"occupation":"Brothel sex worker and evening entertainer","primaryLocationId":"38b0efd4-b1d9-5b32-bc1f-b0b711da47ca","districtId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","homeId":"22ffb750-29ad-52b5-845d-6a2353cd16f6","ageBand":"18-22","biography":"Bess is twenty-one and works at the Red Sash as a sex worker and evening entertainer. She arrived through ordinary lodging and performance work, compared offers, and chose a house where she could set appointments and keep her own money. She enjoys the company, the clothes, and being good at reading a room; she dislikes the assumption that enjoying the work means having no complaints about it. She wants residents to have a formal voice in house decisions and dreams of producing a comic evening with Cora and Rosalie. Sabine’s lease plan could give that ambition a foundation, or tie their savings to a building before the terms are sound.","appearance":"Fair skin with freckles, hazel eyes, thick auburn hair pinned with a red ribbon, and an expressive smile. During public evening hours she favors a fitted burgundy dress with a high lace collar, brass earrings, and polished ankle boots; off duty she wears a practical cream blouse and olive skirt.","personalityTraits":["lively","observant","independent","generous","impatient with condescension"],"interests":["comic songs","theater costumes","cards for amusement","river picnics","small-business ideas"],"quirk":"She tries out a new comic line on friends and keeps a mental tally of who laughed out of politeness.","psychology":{"worldview":"Being paid for one kind of company does not give anyone a claim on the rest of a person’s life.","innerContradiction":"She demands that her judgment be taken seriously and sometimes treats a cautious question as an attempt to manage her.","coreInsecurity":"Discovering that a promise of independence has made her dependent on somebody else’s private favor.","desire":"Secure a real say in the house, produce an evening of her own material, and have relationships chosen outside a booking book.","complication":"A short lease window, uneven savings, and an urge to announce a plan before the less glamorous terms are settled.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"She has a conditional offer to join a traveling entertainment company and has not told Sabine because she fears it will make her support for the house look insincere."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Bright, direct, and quick with a practical joke. She can be frankly flirtatious when interested, but her clearest emotional moments drop the performance and ask a simple question.","openingLine":"If you have come for the music, I can promise a tune. If you have come with assumptions, leave a few by the door.","casualLine":"Cora says the chorus needs another verse. Sabine says the evening needs a budget. This is why a person requires several kinds of friend.","conflictLine":"I enjoy my work. I am still allowed to object to the terms. You need to hear both sentences.","earnedAffectionLine":"I am off duty, and I asked you here because I wanted you. It matters to me that you understand the difference.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Confident banter, clear invitations, shared amusement, and an off-duty intimacy that becomes increasingly candid. Paid appointments and personal attraction are separately established; professional warmth does not prove romantic interest.","boundaries":"A booking grants only the agreed appointment and can be declined or ended. Gifts, money, rescue narratives, and a request for exclusivity do not purchase private affection or a change of occupation. Any exclusive relationship requires a specific discussion of work and expectations.","expressionTier":"confident and forward","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"21c924ca-f314-5503-ad27-3e741169f6b6","text":"Her first successful comic song earned more laughter than she expected, and she forgot the final line because she was enjoying herself.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"6c99deef-105d-52b8-b38e-aea19a47f094","text":"Mabel once asked what she wanted from a contract before offering advice; Bess remembers the question as the more valuable gift.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["review her own appointment choices","rehearse songs and comic material","prepare public parlor clothing and personal space","host conversation and entertainment","attend agreed private appointments with details off page","close personal accounts and meet residents"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["83833b22-7a11-59ac-b4ee-27cea0e3c35b","1a511bfe-6c6d-5942-bbae-6f85fa2a7217","7e80c107-194e-5283-9f41-8964f282e145"],"schedulePattern":"evening","factionAssociations":["lantern-business-circle"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["3d27cafb-1dd2-5174-acd8-ed98fd3bac24","01bb2e94-4d1e-50d2-a7e7-1a7c8674912c","697dd0d0-9889-5eed-bd03-a8f47915cec6","f9a1ebe3-647f-5004-aab9-c412bbfae74c","817b77d0-add0-536f-9c20-51ba63f7c072","ccb6fc6c-77e2-51ba-82bf-30c410de85fa","4622e5fc-35c9-5d01-849f-cee3633ffe7a","8198d98c-c4fd-55b7-949f-8b6e5e498516","92c195b5-8d84-55dd-82ba-855614e1773e","4e41a762-f146-5a4b-8c4a-9a8c09d7a19d"],"storyArcIds":["eabfaee1-1df0-54ec-9183-b31adaaafea9","15ed8e86-a592-5680-985a-f42ab39a00c5"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at The Red Sash.","Being paid for one kind of company does not give anyone a claim on the rest of a person’s life.","Direct experience of late mornings belong to staff and deliveries. rehearsal and preparation grow into crowded evenings; closing-time meals create their own community."],"personalHistory":["3d27cafb-1dd2-5174-acd8-ed98fd3bac24","01bb2e94-4d1e-50d2-a7e7-1a7c8674912c","697dd0d0-9889-5eed-bd03-a8f47915cec6","f9a1ebe3-647f-5004-aab9-c412bbfae74c","817b77d0-add0-536f-9c20-51ba63f7c072","ccb6fc6c-77e2-51ba-82bf-30c410de85fa","4622e5fc-35c9-5d01-849f-cee3633ffe7a","8198d98c-c4fd-55b7-949f-8b6e5e498516","92c195b5-8d84-55dd-82ba-855614e1773e","4e41a762-f146-5a4b-8c4a-9a8c09d7a19d"],"privateFactId":"5311c57e-c7ed-5702-8ed2-3d640f6a9532","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Bess Kincaid, an adult 21-year-old woman, Scottish American, brothel sex worker and evening entertainer, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Fair skin with freckles, hazel eyes, thick auburn hair pinned with a red ribbon, and an expressive smile. During public evening hours she favors a fitted burgundy dress with a high lace collar, brass earrings, and polished ankle boots; off duty she wears a practical cream blouse and olive skirt. At the visitor-facing part of The Red Sash. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-bess-kincaid","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"character:9ed8bf33-40ad-580c-baff-ce50e70870e7","content_type":"character_canon","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"9ed8bf33-40ad-580c-baff-ce50e70870e7","authoringNumber":49,"worldId":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","slug":"sabine-roche","name":"Sabine Roche","age":26,"gender":"woman","heritage":"French American","spiceLevel":3,"occupation":"Brothel sex worker and resident accounts representative","primaryLocationId":"38b0efd4-b1d9-5b32-bc1f-b0b711da47ca","districtId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","homeId":"0a36f4ff-4010-5a1b-98d1-6b3e427d9cf9","ageBand":"23-50","biography":"Sabine is twenty-six, a sex worker at the Red Sash and the residents’ chosen representative for shared accounts. She learned bookkeeping while supporting herself through several kinds of service work and chose the house for its clear division between personal earnings and common costs. She likes the work when the terms are hers. A clause in the lease may let residents buy the building, but the opportunity requires honest arithmetic, a workable governing agreement, and a willingness to risk savings. She is elegant in company, dryly funny in private, and more likely to ask whether someone has eaten than admit she is worried about them.","appearance":"Medium brown skin, dark amber eyes, black curls gathered in a careful updo, and an unhurried, poised bearing. Deep teal or plum dresses with neat cuffs, a narrow gold locket, and well-kept practical shoes; her desk always has an apron or plain work shawl nearby.","personalityTraits":["perceptive","composed","pragmatic","loyal","guarded about dependence"],"interests":["bookkeeping","French novels","cooking","potted herbs","musical evenings"],"quirk":"She straightens a column of figures when she is deciding how much of a feeling to say aloud.","psychology":{"worldview":"Freedom lasts longer when its terms can survive an ordinary bad month.","innerContradiction":"She wants shared ownership while finding it difficult to share a decision she believes she understands best.","coreInsecurity":"Losing other people’s savings through a plan that felt safer because she was the one explaining it.","desire":"Build a resident-owned house with fair terms, a reserve for hard months, and room for a private life beyond being everyone’s reliable person.","complication":"Financing pressure, an incomplete ownership agreement, and her temptation to solve the residents’ doubts with reassurance before the figures justify it.","authorOnlyPrivateTruth":"Her first purchase projection omitted two repair costs; she has corrected it privately but has not yet shown residents how much the reserve requirement must rise."},"voice":{"cadenceAndRegister":"Measured and warmly exact, with understated humor. She asks a precise question when somebody is evading one and speaks more simply when the subject is her own desire.","openingLine":"You may ask what the house offers. I may ask what you mean. Clear terms make for much better company.","casualLine":"Bess has written another chorus. I have found another repair bill. We are both contributing to the life of the establishment.","conflictLine":"I corrected the figures. I have not yet done the harder part, which is admit why I preferred the earlier answer.","earnedAffectionLine":"You have asked what would help. Tonight I would like to be wanted without being useful first.","rules":["Use this character’s vocabulary and attention, without phonetic accent spelling.","Make room for ordinary humor and interests beyond the main conflict.","Do not substitute the generic world accent for the authored individual voice."]},"relationship":{"style":"Assured attraction expressed through attentive conversation, deliberate invitations, private humor, and practical tenderness. Trust deepens when a partner can hear uncertainty without taking over or demanding reassurance.","boundaries":"Professional appointments and personal relationships have separate terms. She will not share another resident’s records, surrender financial judgment to a patron, or promise romantic exclusivity by implication. Work remains her choice; affection does not require a different occupation.","expressionTier":"confident and forward","playerRoute":"Available to an adult player character where mutual attraction is established; no player gender or orientation is presumed.","baseline":"No current exclusive partnership blocks a player route. Past relationships and family ties retain their authored meaning.","progress":["recognition through repeated ordinary contact","mutual interest named or invited","private confidence voluntarily offered","affection and expectations discussed","a continuing relationship that permits independent choices"],"professionDoesNotImplyConsent":true,"kinshipCharacterIds":[]},"anecdotes":[{"id":"a992c46e-0299-58f7-af55-11ee28aea55d","text":"A landlady once returned an overpayment without being asked, teaching her that reliable arithmetic could also be a kind of care.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."},{"id":"a42d146e-e0f8-5a21-8a14-7b05c7db4c7d","text":"She and Bess spent a rainy afternoon failing to grow herbs in an ornamental pot and still argue affectionately over whose idea the drainage was.","revealGate":"A relevant topic and this character’s willingness to share; not automatically public biography."}],"workActivities":["review shared costs and repair quotations","confirm her chosen appointments","prepare private rooms and parlor supplies","host agreed conversation and company","hold resident account discussions","close shared books with individual earnings kept private"],"weeklyLeisureAnchorIds":["15e01963-8be0-5523-b708-90c6ed3f5ad3","1382bb5d-2704-5ff2-a0b4-23707e0219e3","fd31aebd-9627-5eb6-aa48-992466e453ee"],"schedulePattern":"evening","factionAssociations":["lantern-business-circle"],"factionRule":"Association, employment, or participation is not unconditional loyalty or formal membership in every institution.","connectionIds":["0070de4d-17cb-551f-a7d0-df4ae15ae525","e7847d80-2cab-5ec7-86cd-d8e4709e5bb5","61d39f75-c2ef-505d-bdec-faee9c840f2a","3be052b9-79ae-5455-b298-ca4a213d20d6","57e802b9-9800-53a1-b844-4138a2a4f30d","ce9a13c4-f2d5-5745-88a8-b9199c847406","b5e39214-058e-5967-9ae5-490cf05f6011","48068021-76b1-5643-b211-2ab9a4893b5e","843960f3-99d2-5bfa-ab5b-309f96995e2a","5db1f14c-4030-5b8a-83fc-00d244c5f947","bfb1275b-5b54-5c5e-88e8-e988a308196c"],"storyArcIds":["15ed8e86-a592-5680-985a-f42ab39a00c5"],"knowledgeSurface":{"public":["Their own occupation at The Red Sash.","Freedom lasts longer when its terms can survive an ordinary bad month.","Direct experience of late mornings belong to staff and deliveries. rehearsal and preparation grow into crowded evenings; closing-time meals create their own community."],"personalHistory":["0070de4d-17cb-551f-a7d0-df4ae15ae525","e7847d80-2cab-5ec7-86cd-d8e4709e5bb5","61d39f75-c2ef-505d-bdec-faee9c840f2a","3be052b9-79ae-5455-b298-ca4a213d20d6","57e802b9-9800-53a1-b844-4138a2a4f30d","ce9a13c4-f2d5-5745-88a8-b9199c847406","b5e39214-058e-5967-9ae5-490cf05f6011","48068021-76b1-5643-b211-2ab9a4893b5e","843960f3-99d2-5bfa-ab5b-309f96995e2a","5db1f14c-4030-5b8a-83fc-00d244c5f947","bfb1275b-5b54-5c5e-88e8-e988a308196c"],"privateFactId":"da89a5c1-4092-53f6-b8c8-c3d7705fc107","exclusions":["Other characters’ hidden facts, client or patient records, sealed messages, and private rooms remain unknown without a supported disclosure.","A public rumor is attributed to a speaker and is not promoted to fact by repetition.","Remember only events the character witnessed, was told, or can establish from available records."]},"portraitPrompt":"Single portrait of Sabine Roche, an adult 26-year-old woman, French American, brothel sex worker and resident accounts representative, fictional territorial Southwest, 1888. Medium brown skin, dark amber eyes, black curls gathered in a careful updo, and an unhurried, poised bearing. Deep teal or plum dresses with neat cuffs, a narrow gold locket, and well-kept practical shoes; her desk always has an apron or plain work shawl nearby. At the visitor-facing part of The Red Sash. Fully clothed, occupation-specific styling, natural posture, one person, no text, no collage. Preserve stated age and distinctive appearance.","asset":{"key":"calders-run-sabine-roche","status":"not_generated"}},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:2873dcbb-5c07-57af-b54e-79806be121cc","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"2873dcbb-5c07-57af-b54e-79806be121cc","category":"district","text":"Permanent brick arrived after the first silver profits. Shopkeepers widened the boardwalks while moving older stalls downhill. The courthouse occupies an expanded reading-room building, and its piecemeal construction is visible from the alley.","locationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:3f3bb467-b257-59be-a080-f2dd65dc3ac2","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"3f3bb467-b257-59be-a080-f2dd65dc3ac2","category":"district","text":"Freight and shopping dominate morning; court business and repairs fill afternoon; hotel balconies and supper visits soften the evening.","locationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:0b98de05-c1e0-5c4c-8711-895a586da3b4","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"0b98de05-c1e0-5c4c-8711-895a586da3b4","category":"district","text":"Shop staff exchange small change and errands before the first coach arrival.","locationId":"8ea973d5-94fe-5c5c-8cb3-84a90abef76e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:1734dc69-22db-5835-a433-84f7be2383c9","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"1734dc69-22db-5835-a433-84f7be2383c9","category":"district","text":"Temporary drinking rooms gave way to purpose-built businesses when miners began receiving regular pay. Adult establishments and theaters funded improvements that more respectable neighbors also use.","locationId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:76fc033b-dfb1-52d4-a7da-cf3d95221cb9","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"76fc033b-dfb1-52d4-a7da-cf3d95221cb9","category":"district","text":"Late mornings belong to staff and deliveries. Rehearsal and preparation grow into crowded evenings; closing-time meals create their own community.","locationId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:ac6ebc71-dae7-53f1-8c57-488b109b696e","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"ac6ebc71-dae7-53f1-8c57-488b109b696e","category":"district","text":"After a difficult night, staff send a plate from the Night Kitchen to the business still closing.","locationId":"604a7a05-0d7e-5ea2-9357-1e9953bf3bd1","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:526b3cab-0a7b-517a-bbbd-bf907661ba67","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"526b3cab-0a7b-517a-bbbd-bf907661ba67","category":"district","text":"The flood erased several streets but not their households. Rebuilt walls contain salvaged material; the headworks and ferry compact are part of family history.","locationId":"4331f47a-a84a-5a9c-84bb-29e462d61985","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:9c74cce5-c449-5859-aeac-aa2c094f5813","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"9c74cce5-c449-5859-aeac-aa2c094f5813","category":"district","text":"Early departures, clinic and market business, afternoon repairs, and communal supper create frequent encounters across occupations.","locationId":"4331f47a-a84a-5a9c-84bb-29e462d61985","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:87a14d15-338d-5fbf-965a-43df9a969439","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"87a14d15-338d-5fbf-965a-43df9a969439","category":"district","text":"People leave dry boards near doors for arrivals with wet boots.","locationId":"4331f47a-a84a-5a9c-84bb-29e462d61985","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:c8c6b581-3a21-5a22-9116-e5a082343730","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"c8c6b581-3a21-5a22-9116-e5a082343730","category":"district","text":"Last year’s survey camp is already a depot, supply street, office compound, and growing settlement. Its residents resent being treated as visitors to the west-bank town.","locationId":"b825b72f-5bd8-5f53-a5a3-e4b862932ae7","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:6d37f443-dd99-57a2-8d3d-3710492b812a","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"6d37f443-dd99-57a2-8d3d-3710492b812a","category":"district","text":"Dispatch and deliveries begin early. Survey and bridge crews move through daylight; correspondence and repairs continue after passenger activity slows.","locationId":"b825b72f-5bd8-5f53-a5a3-e4b862932ae7","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:b90696f2-73db-5379-b1be-78dcfdf046db","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"b90696f2-73db-5379-b1be-78dcfdf046db","category":"district","text":"The day’s first passenger arrival is checked from the provisioner’s porch with mugs in hand.","locationId":"b825b72f-5bd8-5f53-a5a3-e4b862932ae7","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:686d57cc-5677-53e4-a103-0a4a2d8780cb","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"686d57cc-5677-53e4-a103-0a4a2d8780cb","category":"district","text":"Several patterns of cultivation precede the modern town. The water register overlays older practices imperfectly, and later ranch consolidation has never settled every claim.","locationId":"cff3d4a7-0a30-57e0-ba3f-d74db9b72810","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:773f327f-097f-5eb1-86e4-a5b176dc9857","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"773f327f-097f-5eb1-86e4-a5b176dc9857","category":"district","text":"Animals and irrigation require early work; afternoons shift toward repair and household business; evening brings adult lessons, porch visits, and shared meals.","locationId":"cff3d4a7-0a30-57e0-ba3f-d74db9b72810","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:8846869e-e35c-560f-a500-e5b5ce8e53df","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"8846869e-e35c-560f-a500-e5b5ce8e53df","category":"district","text":"At the first cool evening after a hot spell, households bring food to the meeting-house yard.","locationId":"cff3d4a7-0a30-57e0-ba3f-d74db9b72810","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:1277dd0b-aa1a-59e1-bf11-acc4f382f694","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"1277dd0b-aa1a-59e1-bf11-acc4f382f694","category":"district","text":"Commercial silver connected scattered routes and camps. The 1881 collapse left a mutual society, a cemetery expansion, and unresolved arguments about responsibility.","locationId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:394acae2-4e65-503a-ab73-fa4c2a01409f","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"394acae2-4e65-503a-ab73-fa4c2a01409f","category":"district","text":"Mining and travel start early. Supply exchanges fill midday; late arrivals gather at stations and trading rooms before the roads become difficult.","locationId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:4f034df6-324e-5e8f-b6b4-0d1552bbb6cc","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"4f034df6-324e-5e8f-b6b4-0d1552bbb6cc","category":"district","text":"A returned traveler is offered water before being asked for news.","locationId":"4aa276e2-1323-53a9-b9eb-d8de7cf3547e","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:a6cc58aa-d78e-58fa-a768-69f2f8fdc2ec","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"a6cc58aa-d78e-58fa-a768-69f2f8fdc2ec","category":"history","text":"Before 1859 — Routes before the town: Indigenous movement, older Mexican households, small-scale cultivation, and local irrigation precede the freight settlement. Specific communities have continuing interests; the river is not empty land awaiting discovery.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:20cfc3f6-3f28-52c2-a243-9e7c14a83256","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"20cfc3f6-3f28-52c2-a243-9e7c14a83256","category":"history","text":"1859 — Calder’s Run: Amelia Calder organizes a reliable freight-and-ferry circuit. The route lends its name to the settlement; the ferry book begins as a practical business record.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:f6346a01-c06e-52b1-8432-2d9cd626f2fa","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"f6346a01-c06e-52b1-8432-2d9cd626f2fa","category":"history","text":"1864 — Silver in the bluffs: Commercial workings expand at what becomes Saint Agnes. Supply yards and modest lodging follow the workers.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:b9408089-3a6b-517a-af01-1d8911c82cfa","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"b9408089-3a6b-517a-af01-1d8911c82cfa","category":"history","text":"1868 — A permanent Main Street: Brick businesses replace several temporary fronts. A public reading room becomes the first court-record office.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:ba9bebc1-5052-5827-a642-97c485794850","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"ba9bebc1-5052-5827-a642-97c485794850","category":"history","text":"1872 — The high-water year: Flooding damages River Ward and destroys a portion of county records. Collective rebuilding creates both solidarity and disputed obligations.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:96c6998f-d390-57da-b930-7f9cebd58831","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"96c6998f-d390-57da-b930-7f9cebd58831","category":"history","text":"1874 — The crossing compact: A local trusteeship formalizes ferry maintenance, public headworks, and registered water turns. Emergency advantages become durable privileges.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:d32a9214-e672-5d1a-8241-58f45f13bbb9","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"d32a9214-e672-5d1a-8241-58f45f13bbb9","category":"history","text":"1877 — Lantern Row expands: A theater, larger saloon rooms, and independent adult businesses make evening trade a substantial employer.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:53583382-d088-5fef-a7bd-b3fc18266e5e","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"53583382-d088-5fef-a7bd-b3fc18266e5e","category":"history","text":"1881 — The Saint Agnes collapse: A shaft failure kills and injures workers. The miners’ mutual-aid fund forms; contemporary liability remains contested.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:5a53ea45-4912-5e6c-9d43-4c591f9b836f","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"5a53ea45-4912-5e6c-9d43-4c591f9b836f","category":"history","text":"1883 — The relay revival: Older freight routes return to use as private couriers exploit demand for cheaper and less scrutinized transport.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:1d97b4e9-3b84-50cb-ba2c-b7d69c71fd38","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"1d97b4e9-3b84-50cb-ba2c-b7d69c71fd38","category":"history","text":"1885 — The dry summer: Low water exposes inequalities in the allocation register. Small growers begin sharing copies of schedules and delivery receipts.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:7560a609-e6d0-53dc-96a4-ce8f4a98ab7b","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"7560a609-e6d0-53dc-96a4-ce8f4a98ab7b","category":"history","text":"1887 — Survey stakes: Railway surveying raises land prices and rental speculation before many affected tenants know the likely route.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:d733c5d8-e7ae-55c3-b855-2502936aaee5","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"d733c5d8-e7ae-55c3-b855-2502936aaee5","category":"history","text":"1888 — The east-bank terminus: The temporary depot opens. Bridge work begins under limited construction authority; the full franchise remains undecided.","locationId":null,"audience":"public_history_with_stated_uncertainties","knownByCharacterIds":[],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:c6cfad2b-4fd1-58b1-9a89-6186c28da6e7","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"c6cfad2b-4fd1-58b1-9a89-6186c28da6e7","category":"place","text":"A three-story brick hotel with a shaded balcony, dependable meals, and a lobby where visitors learn how quickly an arrival becomes public news.","locationId":"6091676c-6511-5aa5-81a4-6582b38dbc30","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["a71259b6-01ca-57c1-b8f6-1f4a2ed5d8d3"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:4e53a77c-bba3-527d-b0e2-250250bec6ae","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"4e53a77c-bba3-527d-b0e2-250250bec6ae","category":"place_private","text":"Rafael has quietly reserved one low-priced room for stranded travelers using gratuities of his own. Management has not authorized a permanent relief arrangement.","locationId":"6091676c-6511-5aa5-81a4-6582b38dbc30","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["a71259b6-01ca-57c1-b8f6-1f4a2ed5d8d3"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:ef1bd09a-64e0-5294-82b6-bcaa8c4eb3e9","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"ef1bd09a-64e0-5294-82b6-bcaa8c4eb3e9","category":"place","text":"A working print shop publishing The Run Ledger, selling stationery, and turning private grievances into carefully chosen public words.","locationId":"b8e6063d-69c1-5791-bb0d-595e8ea26148","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["63a4bf14-598c-509f-861f-46a1ce3c729b"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:dca265e6-f54c-5c9b-9374-1200b506d2e9","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"dca265e6-f54c-5c9b-9374-1200b506d2e9","category":"place_private","text":"A local patron offered to clear Iris’s equipment debt in exchange for advance sight of articles. The proposal remains unanswered in her private correspondence.","locationId":"b8e6063d-69c1-5791-bb0d-595e8ea26148","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["63a4bf14-598c-509f-861f-46a1ce3c729b"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:662b8362-a947-54bd-8c35-b52958ee6b00","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"662b8362-a947-54bd-8c35-b52958ee6b00","category":"place","text":"The county’s modest record office and hearing rooms, where property, inheritance, and public promises acquire forms that outlast the people arguing over them.","locationId":"12a6914f-0fe4-544d-bfe9-b36c97ea81e8","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["17799880-e679-5080-b921-b9f4afa3b6fb"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:68999dd9-929f-53e5-a6fd-9089dc277b7f","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"68999dd9-929f-53e5-a6fd-9089dc277b7f","category":"place_private","text":"A copied water-register page combines measurements from different years. Its existence is genuine; whether its use was fraudulent requires comparison with other evidence.","locationId":"12a6914f-0fe4-544d-bfe9-b36c97ea81e8","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["17799880-e679-5080-b921-b9f4afa3b6fb"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:f56f6bd9-1dc3-5feb-bb7a-8633b0a877a0","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"f56f6bd9-1dc3-5feb-bb7a-8633b0a877a0","category":"place","text":"A busy livery and training yard where the town hires transport, boards animals, swaps practical news, and learns whether a newcomer can be trusted with a horse.","locationId":"602be10b-b09b-58df-965e-033a1ea401d8","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["db699624-91b3-5c34-93ec-53c7974498fb"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:7b72084a-f6f2-518d-a24c-0ba486500b5c","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"7b72084a-f6f2-518d-a24c-0ba486500b5c","category":"place_private","text":"A recently accepted boarding animal matches a disputed bill of sale. June knows the paperwork is weak but has not established who is telling the truth.","locationId":"602be10b-b09b-58df-965e-033a1ea401d8","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["db699624-91b3-5c34-93ec-53c7974498fb"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:1f3bfa0f-fd6c-5e65-8c0c-22aee9754261","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"1f3bfa0f-fd6c-5e65-8c0c-22aee9754261","category":"place","text":"The mercantile supplies everything from nails and lamp wicks to fabric, with a stockroom whose contents reveal the town’s changing ambitions.","locationId":"3c7e94d9-4f78-56e4-bc3c-d40056fbfb49","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["38c61131-14a4-5a14-9165-d307095419ba"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:81dddb89-b640-5a20-80de-e1ad3e006fdb","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"81dddb89-b640-5a20-80de-e1ad3e006fdb","category":"place_private","text":"Lottie has designed a buying list for a small independent shop. She is using public catalog prices, not stealing the store’s accounts.","locationId":"3c7e94d9-4f78-56e4-bc3c-d40056fbfb49","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["38c61131-14a4-5a14-9165-d307095419ba"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:61280a72-dd38-5721-83c0-f6d54d384413","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"61280a72-dd38-5721-83c0-f6d54d384413","category":"place","text":"A warm bakery serving ordinary bread, occasional elaborate pastries, and a few tables whose regulars know the rhythms of the oven.","locationId":"9fcae9c7-e773-534c-9ac7-7df82b66ae17","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["2005abeb-d903-5a5a-a1cb-296fdd68b02a"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:8b2efa87-1585-589c-b3b3-c34151441b6b","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"8b2efa87-1585-589c-b3b3-c34151441b6b","category":"place_private","text":"Beatrice keeps a small, openly documented reduced-price shelf after the main rush. She is ashamed that she sometimes resents customers who assume the reduction is endless.","locationId":"9fcae9c7-e773-534c-9ac7-7df82b66ae17","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["2005abeb-d903-5a5a-a1cb-296fdd68b02a"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:70dd3cb1-fb0f-53a7-bd52-9b7efe01f3b1","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"70dd3cb1-fb0f-53a7-bd52-9b7efe01f3b1","category":"place","text":"The marshal’s small office combines public service, uncomfortable waiting, local records, and the persistent problem of deciding which trouble cannot wait.","locationId":"44c76f68-9a74-55b2-ba70-fe46da0742f6","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:f5b3e52d-5124-54ca-bb4f-36e53d2ba889","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"f5b3e52d-5124-54ca-bb4f-36e53d2ba889","category":"place_private","text":"Elias has tolerated limited fee-evasion deliveries when household necessity was involved. His notes distinguish those cases, but the arrangement was never formally approved.","locationId":"44c76f68-9a74-55b2-ba70-fe46da0742f6","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["dc689ec4-8705-5bcc-80f2-00d8c2180e6a"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:f038bb97-ee40-50b6-9b9e-2d958438a51d","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"f038bb97-ee40-50b6-9b9e-2d958438a51d","category":"place","text":"A forge and wagon yard where hot metal, measured workmanship, and friendly argument keep the town’s animals and vehicles moving.","locationId":"5bd7111c-2e34-5c40-9779-b4dd2aec21c3","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["55a8bac4-eb22-50e5-ae50-84704e68caab"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:be3651e9-efe3-5a72-9c80-4f3f5867c526","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"be3651e9-efe3-5a72-9c80-4f3f5867c526","category":"place_private","text":"Gabriel has priced a new workshop near the railhead but has not told June because she would read the move as a judgment on the livery’s future.","locationId":"5bd7111c-2e34-5c40-9779-b4dd2aec21c3","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["55a8bac4-eb22-50e5-ae50-84704e68caab"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:bd6c427a-862b-55c8-8716-d6c78fec2f2b","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"public","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"bd6c427a-862b-55c8-8716-d6c78fec2f2b","category":"place","text":"The Copper Mare is a generous, noisy saloon with good music, ordinary food, and a back room where people who dislike one another sometimes manage to talk.","locationId":"e0526a03-fbb9-5eb9-bdbd-31872d63f11b","audience":"public_local_knowledge","knownByCharacterIds":["9ed7daa2-a0a3-52cf-b7f4-ad8d220750ab"],"revealGate":null},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_v1","authoringSchema":"calders-run-authoring-pack-v1"}},{"world_id":"31740169-035e-5b10-8c9d-98b206e9f24b","content_key":"fact:1d8acf28-edcd-5289-8a5e-56a04fb81fc8","content_type":"fact","knowledge_scope":"private","content_level":"standard","payload":{"id":"1d8acf28-edcd-5289-8a5e-56a04fb81fc8","category":"place_private","text":"Gin can purchase the building only with outside money. Halden’s associate wants approval over private bookings in return for favorable financing.","locationId":"e0526a03-fbb9-5eb9-bdbd-31872d63f11b","audience":"author_only_until_disclosed","knownByCharacterIds":["9ed7daa2-a0a3-52cf-b7f4-ad8d220750ab"],"revealGate":"Explicit voluntary disclosure or an authored evidence transition; ownership alone does not reveal another person’s knowledge."},"metadata":{"source":"calders_run_authoring_